PVD("palau_ndp_2023-2026",{"docs":["","Palau NDP 2023 26"],"s":{"1":[[1,"4","5","Performance Monitoring and Financing Framework","The establishment of a Performance Monitoring and Financing Framework, centered on implementation, provides us with a practical tool to confront the challenges hindering Palau's growth and development.",""],[1,"4","5","Development Priority Alignment and Coordination Mechanism","It empowers the government to align development priorities with budget allocations, implement robust performance monitoring mechanisms, and identify areas requiring heightened coordination for development.",""],[1,"6","9","Sector Performance Monitoring and Funding Framework","PDP progress will be annually monitored at the sector level as each sector performance monitoring and funding framework is annually updated every April to May in preparation for budget negotiations.",""],[1,"6","9","End-of-PDP Evaluation","An end-of-PDP evaluation will be prepared and presented",""],[1,"8","3","National Oversight Committee for Plan Preparation","A National Oversight Committee consisting of high-level representatives of National and State Governments as well as non-governmental organizations and other stakeholders oversaw the preparation of the plan.",""],[1,"8","3","Core Group for Inclusive Plan Design and Monitoring","A Core Group of planners and other officials were responsible for incorporating the views of all communities, for plan design and drafting, and for preparing the implementation and progress monitoring of the plan.",""]],"2":[[1,"12","3","State-Owned Enterprise and Public Finance Reform","Reformed State-Owned Enterprises (SOEs), civil service pension fund, social security, and State Government finances.",""]],"4":[[1,"17","3","Clean Potable Water Access Improvement","Improving and stabilizing access to clean, potable water is an immediate priority for all communities.",""],[1,"37","1","Integrated Waste and Chemicals Management Improvements","Improved waste management services, waste reduction, recycling, and landfill operation improved hazardous waste and oil spill management, contaminated site management, and lifecycle chemical tracking, monitoring, and reporting will help reduce pollution of lagoon waters and prevent disease and other public health issues.",""],[1,"37","2","Safe Water Supply and Sanitation Improvement Programmes","Improved access to safe water supplies, improved sanitation programs and sustainable, climate-proof construction will help protect community health and the environment.",""],[1,"39","11","Integrated Waste Management and Recycling Services","Improved waste management services, segregation, composting, and recycling, landfill operations for improved hazardous waste and oil spill management, contaminated site management, rehabilitation of closed dumps, and chemical tracking, monitoring, and reporting will help reduce pollution of lagoon waters and prevent disease and other public health issues.",""],[1,"39","12","Safe Water Supply Improvement","Improved access to safe water supplies, improved sanitation programs and sustainable, climate-proof construction will help protect community health and the environment.",""],[1,"39","12","Sanitation Program Improvement","Improved access to safe water supplies, improved sanitation programs and sustainable, climate-proof construction will help protect community health and the environment.",""],[1,"39","14","Sustainable Environmental Financing and Regulatory Strengthening","Conservation and management of Palau's environment can be supported through sustainable financing, updated environmental policies, strategies, and regulations, improved environmental compliance and enforcement, and increased public participation in environmental management.",""],[1,"59","2","Waste and Pollution Reduction from Dumps and Sewage","Manage and reduce waste and reduce pollution from dumps and sewage.",""],[1,"65","1","Pesticide Residue Monitoring Capacity Enhancement","The Palau Environmental Quality Protection Board (EQPB) licenses pesticide applicators and regulates pesticide use, but needs additional laboratory capacity and resources to be able to monitor levels of pesticide residue and minimize chemical residues (this is addressed in the Environment Sector).",""],[1,"70","27","Compost Facility Capacity Expansion","Double capacity of a compost facility",""]],"5":[[1,"12","3","Land and Labor Policy Reform","New land and labor policies are implemented.",""]],"8":[[1,"147","5","Installation of High-Speed Data Recorders for Fault Analysis","Installation of high-speed data recorders for fault analysis",""],[1,"147","8","Grid-Forming Battery Installation near Koror","Installation of a grid forming battery near Koror",""],[1,"155","23","Grid-Forming Battery Installation near Koror","Installation of a grid forming battery near Koror",""],[1,"149","4","Renewable Energy Public-Private Partnership","The government formed a PPP with EarthX, GridMarket, and the Global Island Partnership (GLISPA) in July 2018 to develop renewable energy in the country.",""],[1,"155","5","Sustainable Power Infrastructure Investment Program","Sustainable investment program for power generation, transmission, and distribution",""],[1,"155","21","High-Speed Data Recorder Installation for Fault Analysis","Installation of high-speed data recorders for fault analysis",""]],"10":[[1,"92","10","NDBP New Building Construction","NDBP requires a new building as it expands its services and client base.",""],[1,"93","29","New Bank Building for NDBP","III.1 New bank building for NDBP to enable expansion of staff and services",""]],"12":[[1,"98","2","Blue Economy Aquaculture Business Development and Market Support","Encouraging more private sector engagement in aquaculture would benefit from the deployment of Blue Economy innovative business models and market development in addition to sustained technical assistance and extension services.",""],[1,"98","2","Aquaculture Hatchery and Research and Training Facility","This hatchery augments seed stock supply for prospective fish farmers and is also utilized as a demonstration and training facility for those in the community who are interested to learn and develop their skills in the seed production of marine organisms.",""],[1,"98","6","Aquaculture Seedling Production Expansion and Decentralization","Continued investment into expansion and decentralization of aquaculture seedling production and training in new species is essential to meet national Blue Prosperity and food security plans.",""],[1,"101","5","Blue Economy Institutional Capacity Building and Training Programme","Build long-term institutional capacity to fill critical \"Blue Economy\" capacity gaps, anticipate emerging needs of the sector, and invest in individuals to effectively lead programs, including investing in extension, capacity building, and training programs for farmers and fishers in fisheries and aquaculture to expand aquaculture production and pelagic fishery production",""]],"13":[[1,"65","7","Digital Marketplace for Local Food Sales","With the investment in the internet, the digital marketplace offers a mechanism by which to connect buyers with sellers to improve sales, reduce waste, and improve efficiency.",""],[1,"65","7","Modernization of Food Sales","Modernizing sales and investing in a digital marketplace, with ongoing digital support, is a priority across the entire food system.",""],[1,"65","8","Food Waste Composting and Food Processing Support","Food waste is significant, and compost is one viable method to recycle the carbon and nutrients in food waste.",""],[1,"66","1","Organic Certification Support for Women-Owned Taro Farms","The first group of women-owned taro farms was certified under the Pacific Organic Standard in 2022.",""],[1,"66","2","Local Food Production and Consumption Campaign","Continued cross-sector coordination, planning, and implementation (via a comprehensive local food production and consumption campaign), combined with detailed data collection and analysis, is needed to ensure that Palau becomes more food secure across its entire food security spectrum (from production through processing and distribution to consumption).",""],[1,"66","2","Modernization of Food Security Monitoring Systems","Monitoring systems need to be modernized and online, which also requires digital training and maintenance.",""],[1,"69","5","Root Crop Processing Commercialization and Diversification Support","Provision of technical support to commercialize and diversify root crop processing",""],[1,"69","6","Online Marketing Mechanism Development","Development of an online marketing mechanism",""],[1,"70","8","Root Crop Packing and Processing Expansion","Expand root crop packing and processing from taro to include tapioca and breadfruit (production of flour, chips, new products, etc.)",""],[1,"70","8","Agricultural Production and Purchasing Data System","Data collection to track production and purchasing.",""],[1,"70","8","Online Agricultural Marketing System","Online marketing system operational with reduced food waste and stable supply and demand pricing",""],[1,"70","21","Organic Certification Program","Organic Certification Program operational (Funded through NGO partners)",""]],"21":[[1,"6","1","Direct Assistance to Small Businesses","direct assistance to small businesses.",""],[1,"60","5","Direct Assistance to Small Businesses","the rural and outer island communities prioritize direct assistance to small businesses.",""],[1,"20","2","Private Investment Attraction Support","This would require a realistic appraisal of and support for potential means to attract new private investment.",""],[1,"30","3","Attract Overseas Palauans Through Skilled Job Creation","Palauans currently living overseas could be attracted to return to work in the country if skilled and higher salaried positions were created through increased private investment and domestic economic activity.",""],[1,"20","3","Government Labor Policy Statement","A government statement of labor policy would help clarify future employment needs, associated education and training requirements, the government's position on immigration, support for new labor standards, and labor rights, and better direct the required labor market legislation and regulations.",""],[1,"30","4","Government Labor Policy Statement","A government statement of labor policy would help clarify future employment needs, associated education and training requirements, the government's position on immigration, support for new labor standards, and labor rights, and better direct the required labor market legislation and regulations.",""],[1,"31","3","Development Policy Coordination","This requires a sustained commitment to the coordination of development policy.",""],[1,"31","3","Immigration Control Policy","It has long been government policy in Palau to seek to control immigration, to place direct controls on foreign investment, and to implement programs to encourage the return of Palauans living, working, and studying overseas.",""],[1,"31","3","Foreign Investment Controls","It has long been government policy in Palau to seek to control immigration, to place direct controls on foreign investment, and to implement programs to encourage the return of Palauans living, working, and studying overseas.",""],[1,"31","3","Diaspora Return Incentive Programmes","It has long been government policy in Palau to seek to control immigration, to place direct controls on foreign investment, and to implement programs to encourage the return of Palauans living, working, and studying overseas.",""],[1,"40","1","Economic and Structural Reform Program","The government has already committed to a wide-ranging program of economic and structural reform, and this will help secure government finances and strengthen the economy.",""],[1,"41","5","Agriculture and Fisheries Commercial Investment and Development Policies","New agriculture and fisheries commercial investment and development policies are needed to support more diverse growth and development.",""],[1,"43","6","Agriculture and Fisheries Commercial Investment and Development Policies","New agriculture and fisheries commercial investment and development policies are needed to support diversified growth and development.",""],[1,"41","5","Out-grower and Contracting Schemes for Commercial Agriculture","Out-grower and contracting schemes may hold some potential for commercial agriculture development and scaling up the current small day-boat fleet offers some potential for commercial fisheries development (footnote 53).",""],[1,"41","5","Scaling Up the Small Day-Boat Fleet","Out-grower and contracting schemes may hold some potential for commercial agriculture development and scaling up the current small day-boat fleet offers some potential for commercial fisheries development (footnote 53).",""],[1,"43","2","Private Enterprise Support Package for Rural Communities","State Governments and NGO partners can support the development of private enterprise through a suite of actions, ranging from the creation of markets (physical and literal), more secure land and aquaculture leases, construction of food processing centers, and facilitation of support services such as business planning and loan application help for the most vulnerable community members.",""],[1,"43","2","Expanded State Support Services for Small Entrepreneurs","Expanding the state's capacity to offer these support services to small entrepreneurs, especially those in food production, is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"43","4","Industrial and Marine Hub Development and Investment Promotion","the attraction of large and small businesses to existing and new industrial, business, and marine hubs by providing land, water access, and infrastructure and through active promotion and negotiation is a medium- to long-term priority.",""],[1,"43","4","Foreign Investment Attraction Initiative","Obtaining foreign investment is another immediate priority for Airai and Aimeliik.",""],[1,"44","2","Small Business and Entrepreneurial Support Capacity Strengthening","The capacity of State Governments and partners should be strengthened to provide small business and entrepreneurial support, particularly in the food production sectors.",""],[1,"50","1","Small Business Advisory and Financial Assistance","The Small Business Development Center and the National Development Bank of Palau will continue to provide advisory and financial assistance to small businesses.",""],[1,"50","1","Support Services Expansion for Small Entrepreneurs","Expanding the state's capacity to offer these support services to small entrepreneurs, especially those in food production, is an immediate priority for these state communities.",""],[1,"50","1","Investment Promotion Development Unit","The Ministries of Finance (MOF), Human Resources, Culture, Tourism and Development, and Public Infrastructure and Industries plan to jointly create a Development Unit for investment promotion.","Ministries of Finance (MOF), Human Resources, Culture, Tourism and Development, and Public Infrastructure and Industries"],[1,"50","1","E-commerce and FinTech Development Support","MOF also plans to support the further development of e-commerce and FinTech.","MOF"],[1,"50","2","Private Sector Development Strategy","The government will work with representatives of the private sector, including foreign investors, to list, detail, and prioritize remaining issues of concern, and then to jointly work through these issues with a view to gradually adopting improved policies.",""],[1,"57","7","Private Sector Development Strategy","A private sector development strategy will help improve the environment for investment, commerce, and trade.",""],[1,"50","6","Expansion of State Public Land Lease Programs","Thus, the expansion of lease programs is a medium-term priority for most States.",""],[1,"49","2","Private Sector Investment Climate Reform Package","The government is continuing reforms to improve the environment for private sector investment including foreign direct investment.",""],[1,"49","2","Secured Transactions and Online Registry Reform","Palau has introduced secured transactions law and an online registry.",""],[1,"49","2","Credit Register Assessment","The Government with ADB PSDI support is currently assessing the possibility of introducing a credit register that will assist with reviewing credit applications.",""],[1,"49","2","Domestic Arbitration Policy and Law Development","The government has started policy work on a domestic arbitration policy and law.",""],[1,"49","2","Corporate Registry Modernization","The Ministry of Finance commenced implementation of the new Corporations Law by developing technical specifications to establish a new electronic registry.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"49","3","Private Enterprise Development Support Package","state governments and NGO partners aim to support the development of private enterprise through a suite of actions, ranging from the creation of markets (physical and literal), more secure land and aquaculture leases, construction of food processing centers, and support services such as business planning",""],[1,"59","3","Private Sector Enabling Environment Improvement","Improve private sector productivity by improving the environment for private sector activity.",""],[1,"59","5","Small Business and Entrepreneurship Support","Support small businesses and entrepreneurship.",""],[1,"59","14","Private Sector Growth Strategy","Design and implement a strategy to promote the growth of the private sector.",""],[1,"60","5","Business and Government Performance Improvement Strategies","The country context recognizes the need to design and implement strategies to improve the environments for business and government performance whereas the rural and outer island communities prioritize direct assistance to small businesses.",""]],"22":[[1,"5","4","Palauan Culture Awareness Education Program","the country context focuses on education programs to raise awareness and promote Palauan culture.",""],[1,"5","4","Rural and Outer Islands Cultural Programmes","The rural and outer islands' priorities also focus on offering cultural programs.",""],[1,"5","4","Cultural Sites Restoration and Cultural Centers Network","they prioritize the restoration of cultural sites and providing a functioning network of cultural centers.",""],[1,"18","3","Community Cultural and Environmental Programming","Community priorities for education, therefore, revolve around community cultural and environmental programming to ensure a place-based sense of identity and ongoing sense of stewardship for local resources.",""],[1,"18","3","Intergenerational Knowledge Transfer Initiative","A key priority is to transfer knowledge held by elders to youth.",""],[1,"18","3","Cultural Education Expansion","The expansion of cultural education is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"18","3","Financial Literacy and Business Skills Education","The lack of financial literacy and understanding of business is another concern.",""],[1,"18","4","Capacity Building and Training Programs for Rural and Outer Island Communities","Rural and Outer Island State Governments have prioritized capacity building and training in social and economic sectors for government employees and residents to improve the effectiveness of governance and improve economic conditions.",""],[1,"31","5","Palauan Studies Degree Program","The Palauan Studies 2-year degree program introduced over five years ago at the Palau Community College demonstrates Palau's efforts to ensure cultural sustainability; however, it has failed to attract interest, unlike Western topics and teachings.",""],[1,"32","2","Intergenerational Cultural Knowledge Transfer Programme","The capture and transference of cultural knowledge from the elderly to youth, or from one generation to another, is an immediate priority and could be achieved with minimal investment (see Table 8).",""],[1,"32","2","Community Cultural Programming and Traditional Practices Support","Investment in regular community cultural programming, with support services to document, communicate, and enable traditional practices is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"32","3","Cultural Site Restoration and Maintenance Programme","Relatively low investment in cultural site restoration programs and ongoing investment into site maintenance needs to be addressed and are immediate priorities.",""],[1,"32","3","Cultural Site and Tourism Marketing Alignment","Aligning cultural site programming with tourism marketing is also desired and could build sustainability for maintenance.",""],[1,"32","4","Community, Senior, and Cultural Center Rehabilitation and Accessibility Upgrade","Many communities lack this type of central location, be it a Community Center, Senior Center, or Cultural Center, or their existing centers are in disrepair or are not accessible to elderly populations or handicapped persons.",""],[1,"32","6","Cultural Site Preservation and Cultural Tourism Diversification","Increasing the protection and utilization of cultural sites and practices is a top priority for stakeholders in Koror both to retain culture but also to diversify the economic base.",""],[1,"32","6","Preservation of Taro Patches and Cultural-Historical Sites","Priority sites include the preservation of existing taro patches in Koror (including in the Rock Islands) and cultural and historical sites in the Rock Islands.",""],[1,"32","6","Cultural Tourism Diversification and World Heritage Site Management","A priority for Koror and Airai is to diversify tourism to include cultural tourism, and in Koror, another priority includes better management of, and capitalization of opportunities associated with the World Heritage Site, which was nominated to the UNESCO convention based on both natural and cultural criteria.",""],[1,"32","6","Support for Traditional Fisheries and Gleaning Practices","Supporting traditional practices in fisheries and gleaning is a cultural priority in urban areas.",""],[1,"33","5","Cultural Education Programs and Curricula","Design and support delivery of cultural education programs and curricula that emphasize local knowledge, language, traditions, stories, and heritage for young and old.",""],[1,"33","6","Cultural Site Restoration and Maintenance","Restore and maintain cultural sites to meet local educational and cultural needs while adding value as tourism products.",""],[1,"33","7","Cultural Centers Network Construction and Rehabilitation","Build or repair a network of cultural centers.",""],[1,"33","8","Cultural Site Management Improvement","Improve management of cultural sites in the UNESCO World Heritage site.",""],[1,"37","3","Environmental Education and Cultural Heritage Protection Programme","Environmental education programs that connect habitats and biodiversity to cultural identity and history have been utilized successfully to raise awareness of environmental issues and to build the next generation of environmental stewards.",""],[1,"37","3","Traditional Knowledge Documentation and Heritage Protection Measures","Documentation of traditional knowledge, better protection of cultural heritage, raising public awareness of issues facing natural and cultural heritage, and community and professional education and training programs will help perpetuate Palau's close links between cultural and environmental sustainability.",""],[1,"39","13","Traditional Knowledge and Cultural Heritage Protection Programme","Utilization of traditional knowledge, better protection of cultural heritage, raising public awareness of issues facing natural and cultural heritage, and community and professional education and training programs will help perpetuate Palau's close links between cultural and environmental sustainability.",""],[1,"58","15","Cultural Education Programs and Curriculum Development","Design and support delivery of cultural education programs and curriculum.",""],[1,"58","16","Cultural Programming and Curriculum Development","Offer Cultural programming and curriculum.",""],[1,"58","17","Cultural Centers Network Development","Build, retrofit, or equip a network or Cultural Centers.",""],[1,"58","18","World Heritage Cultural Assets Management","Increase management of cultural assets in the RISL World Heritage site.",""],[1,"60","2","Palauan Culture Awareness Education Programs","the country context focuses on education programs to raise awareness and promote Palauan culture",""],[1,"60","2","Cultural Programs for Rural and Outer Islands","The rural and outer islands' priorities also focus on offering cultural programs",""],[1,"60","2","Cultural Site Restoration and Cultural Centers Network","they also prioritize the restoration of cultural sites and providing a functioning network of cultural centers",""]],"23":[[1,"34","5","Climate Change Adaptation and Mitigation Measures","National climate change responses are focused on adaptation, mitigation, and disaster risk management.",""],[1,"34","5","Cross-Sector Climate Change Mainstreaming","Priority Climate change strategies for natural environments and human settlements and infrastructure are included directly and indirectly across several other PDP sector plans including Energy, Housing, Water and Sanitation, Transportation, Environment, Agriculture, and Fisheries sector plans.",""],[1,"34","5","Climate Adaptation Planning and Financing Support","Ongoing adaptation and planning for climate change are national and sub-national priorities and include strategic planning and adaptation measures, improved access to climate-related financial assistance, and transition to renewable energy sources.",""],[1,"35","2","Fiscal Buffer Building and Contingent Disaster Financing","It has therefore been building fiscal buffers and securing contingent financial assistance from the Asian Development Bank (ADB) to help finance the required future adjustments.",""],[1,"39","2","Climate Change Adaptation and Planning Measures","Ongoing adaptation and planning for climate change include strategic planning and adaptation measures, improved access to climate-related financial assistance, mitigation through a transition to renewable energy sources, energy efficiency, and waste reduction, disaster risk reduction and preparedness, and identification and servicing of vulnerable peoples.",""],[1,"58","20","Disaster and Climate Change Adaptation and Mitigation Program","Programs to adapt, mitigate, and manage disasters and climate change, and enforce environment policies.",""],[1,"59","1","Natural Resource Policy Development","Draft new natural resource policies.",""],[1,"42","7","Fiscal Buffer and Trust Fund Financing","the government also needs to generate increased revenues to fund priority fiscal buffers for natural disasters and climate change, to further establish a \"true\" or \"perpetual\" trust fund, and to restructure the economy.",""],[1,"44","1","Fiscal Revenue Mobilization for Disaster and Climate Buffers","The government also needs to generate increased revenues to fund priority fiscal buffers for natural disasters and climate change, to further capitalize the trust fund, and restructure the economy.",""],[1,"152","11","Programmatic Climate Change Resilience Approach","It introduces new priorities for a programmatic approach to climate change, longer-term capacity",""],[1,"153","3","Disaster-Contingent Financing for Recovery and Reconstruction","Phase 3 of ADB's Pacific Disaster Resilience Program will provide $20 million in disaster-contingent financing for recovery and reconstruction following future natural hazards or health emergencies.",""],[1,"153","5","UN Palau Joint Country Action Plan Support","The 2021 UN Palau Joint Country Action Plan is assisting Palau with (i) climate change, disaster resilience, and environmental protection; (ii) gender equality; (iii) sustainable and inclusive economic empowerment; (iv) equitable basic services; (v) governance and community engagement; and (vi) human rights.",""],[1,"154","2","Mobilization of Multilateral Climate Change Assistance","ensuring greater assistance from multilateral climate change schemes might help to cope with the substantial adaptation cost to prepare for natural disasters and climate change and to finance any proposals for wave energy, solar energy, and other renewable energy projects.",""]],"24":[[1,"86","2","Aquifer Assessment and Sustainable Groundwater Management","there is ongoing work to identify and quantify the value of aquifers and to determine recharge processes and sustainable extraction.",""],[1,"86","2","Freshwater Source Examination for Outer Islands","Further examination of these water sources is needed, especially on outer islands where there are no streams and where sea level rise poses a threat.",""],[1,"86","3","Integrated Watershed Planning, Protection, and Rehabilitation","Integrated land use planning (at the state level) combined with technical watershed planning, protection, and rehabilitation are needed to maintain water quantity and avoid a reduction in water quality, both for human consumption and ecosystem function.",""],[1,"86","4","Water Conservation Education and Outreach","education and outreach on water conservation is a minimal first step",""],[1,"86","4","Watershed Regulation Monitoring and Enforcement","necessitating regular implementation of EQPB's regulations, monitoring, and enforcement",""],[1,"86","4","Water and Soil Laboratory Capacity Expansion","Expanding laboratory capacity to include toxins, chemicals, and minerals in water and soil is needed for Palau to maintain human health",""],[1,"86","4","Expanded Environmental Surveillance and Permit Enforcement","Continued and expanded surveillance and enforcement are also needed to ensure that development permit conditions are implemented and resources important to human health, livelihoods, or the economy are not harmed",""],[1,"88","4","Watershed Rehabilitation and Erosion Control Program","Institutionalizing a program of erosion control, tree planting, or land cover rehabilitation to improve water quality on Babeldaob (for which there is proof of concept) is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"88","4","Outer Islands Aquifer Protection Measures","Improving environmental conditions around aquifers on outer islands is also an immediate priority to protect their extremely limited water supplies.",""],[1,"90","23","Erosion and Water Quality Control Program","II.7 Community: erosion and water quality control program (Babeldaob)",""],[1,"90","9","Environmental Laboratory Capacity Upgrade","Upgraded laboratory capacity to test water and soil",""],[1,"140","3","Land Use Planning and Zoning for Sediment Reduction","Implementation of land use planning and zoning to reduce future sediment inputs is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"140","3","Erosion Control, Tree Planting, and Land Cover Rehabilitation Programme","Institutionalizing a program of erosion control, tree planting, or land cover rehabilitation (for which there is proof of concept) is also an immediate priority.",""],[1,"143","7","Water Quality Monitoring and Sanitation Training","Water quality monitoring and sanitation training.",""],[1,"143","12","Long-Term Water Resource and Chemical Management Investments","Additional longer-term investments will be needed to manage chemicals and determine water-sharing regimes, especially as agriculture expands and if irrigation places a demand on the water during times of drought.",""],[1,"144","15","Water Quality Improvement and Watershed Restoration","Water quality improvements, watershed restoration, pollution prevention, etc.",""],[1,"155","3","Expanded Water Quality Testing Capacity","Expanded water quality testing capacity at EQPB",""],[1,"142","14","Chemical Storage Room Construction","Construction of an additional chemical storage room with AC that can store up to at least 6 months' worth of supplies.",""],[1,"144","7","Chemical Storage Room Construction","Additional Chemical Storage Room constructed.",""],[1,"155","7","Chemical Storage Room Construction and Life Cycle Management Improvement","Construction of additional Chemical Storage Room and improved Life Cycle management",""]],"25":[[1,"120","1","Comprehensive Waste Management System","developing and implementing a comprehensive waste management system with the 3R+Return Policy134 by employing sustainable solutions consistent with traditional and cultural values.",""],[1,"120","4","Waste Segregation Station Collection System","Recently, the Koror State Government (KSG) started implementing a new system for collecting waste from segregation stations.",""],[1,"120","5","M-dock Landfill Management and Rehabilitation","The national government through the Solid Waste Management Office of the Bureau of Public Works (SWM- BPW) is responsible for the management of the M-dock landfill in Koror.","Solid Waste Management Office of the Bureau of Public Works (SWM- BPW)"],[1,"120","5","National Landfill Development in Aimeliik","Only M-dock landfill in Koror and the new national landfill in Aimeliik are designed to minimize environmental impact.",""],[1,"120","5","Medical Waste Incineration at Main Hospital","The main hospital has a high-temperature incinerator to burn medical waste.",""],[1,"120","5","Closure of Open Dumpsites and Alternative Landfill Siting","All other dumpsites are subject to closure soon.",""],[1,"121","3","National Landfill Construction and Relocation Project","The construction of the new national landfill in Aimeliik State has been completed",""],[1,"121","4","Outsourced Waste Collection and Disposal Contract for Babeldaob States","BPW is in the process of outsourcing the waste collection service for Babeldaob States.",""],[1,"121","5","Babeldaob Waste Collection Revolving Fund","A revolving fund finances the Babeldaob waste collection service.",""],[1,"121","6","Dump Restoration, Mitigation, and Capping","restoration, mitigation, and, or capping of dumps is a medium-term priority.",""],[1,"121","8","M-Dock Landfill Operation and Maintenance","Operation and maintenance of M-Dock Landfill.",""],[1,"122","10","Solid Waste Collection Improvement","Solid waste collection is improved in 10 States of Babeldaob Island and in Koror.",""],[1,"123","1","Babeldaob States Waste Collection Service Contract","A service Contract for the Babeldaob States Waste Collection Service is pending.",""],[1,"123","2","Solid Waste Disposal Facilities and Best Practices Upgrade","The government will gradually introduce state-of-the-art facilities and best practices to dispose of solid wastes and thereby promote improved health and preserve the natural environment.",""],[1,"123","3","Closure and Rehabilitation of Disused Waste Disposal Sites","With the construction of the new national landfill in Aimeliik State the older, now disused waste disposal sites need to be closed and the land rehabilitated and returned to commercial or agricultural use, and",""],[1,"124","6","Dump Site Closure Programme","Half of dump sites closed by end of FY27.",""],[1,"152","3","National Landfill Reconstruction","Reconstruction of the national landfill",""]],"65":[[1,"16","3","National Health Insurance Fund","A National Health Insurance Fund launched in 2010 provides universal financial coverage for health care delivered in Palau and subsidized cover for most residents (94% in 2020) for pre- approved off-island care.",""],[1,"16","3","Overseas Referral Care Subsidy System","There is an efficient overseas referral system that subsidizes off-island care through the NHI for services unavailable in Palau.",""]],"66":[[1,"5","3","Non-Communicable Disease Response Programme","the country context priorities are focused on broad programs to improve the quality of education, resolve NCDs, and build a social protection framework.",""]],"68":[[1,"5","3","Social Protection Framework Development","the country context priorities are focused on broad programs to improve the quality of education, resolve NCDs, and build a social protection framework.",""]],"71":[[1,"10","12","Rural State Master Planning Initiative","A new, participatory Rural State Master Planning initiative was launched in 2020 through a GEF64-funded project based at the Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries, and the Environment (MAFE) entitled \"Integrating biodiversity safeguards and conservation into development\" (also known as the Palau Biodiversity Project).","Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries, and the Environment (MAFE)"],[1,"10","12","Land Use Planning and Zoning through Planning Commissions","This initiative combined master planning (identification of goals, objectives, and CIP priorities) with land use planning and zoning, conducted by authorized (and eventually legislated) Planning Commissions.",""],[1,"10","12","Urban and Lagoon Resilience Planning Initiative","Koror began an urban and lagoon resilience planning initiative in early 2022, in partnership with the Great Barrier Reef Foundation, to identify multi-sector development challenges and solutions.",""],[1,"12","2","Climate Change and Disaster Management Investments","Investments that accommodate the environment and climate change.",""],[1,"5","3","Climate Resilience Support Programme","The rural and outer island communities' social priorities revolve around broad programs of assistance, increased climate resilience, and sustainable food security.",""]],"75":[[1,"20","1","Small Business Support for Local Economic Diversification","Supporting small business establishments, particularly in key industries that are needed to ensure social protections such as food security, is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"5","3","Sustainable Food Security Programme","The rural and outer island communities' social priorities revolve around broad programs of assistance, increased climate resilience, and sustainable food security.",""]],"77":[[1,"5","3","Education Quality Improvement Programme","the country context priorities are focused on broad programs to improve the quality of education, resolve NCDs, and build a social protection framework.",""],[1,"17","5","Education Workforce Development Investments","the trend is toward an increasingly educated workforce reflecting investments being made in education workforce development.",""]],"79":[[1,"16","4","Disease Preparedness and Surveillance","Consequently, disease preparedness and surveillance remain sector priorities as well.",""],[1,"17","1","Community Recreational Facilities Expansion","Increasing access to childcare is a medium-term priority for communities.",""],[1,"17","2","Improve Hospital Facilities and Expand Community Medical Staffing","Improving hospital facilities and increasing the number of medical professionals in communities is a long-term priority for communities.",""],[1,"17","2","Outer Islands Transport Improvement","Improving transportation for outer islands, for health and multiple other purposes, is an immediate priority.",""]],"80":[[1,"23","3","Temporary Social Protection Benefit Increase","In response to the COVID-19 pandemic, Palau further increased social protection benefits, albeit on a temporary basis, for both citizens and non-citizens who lost income due to the near cessation of the tourism industry.",""],[1,"24","1","Expansion of Low-Cost Childcare Options","Low-income families with children, especially single-parent households, could benefit from an expansion of low-cost childcare options, targeted labor market support to assist parents to prepare for and find work, and transfer payments to help families respond to crises and rise above the poverty line.",""],[1,"24","1","Targeted Labor Market Support for Parents","Low-income families with children, especially single-parent households, could benefit from an expansion of low-cost childcare options, targeted labor market support to assist parents to prepare for and find work, and transfer payments to help families respond to crises and rise above the poverty line.",""],[1,"26","1","Targeted Labor Market Support for Parents","these families could benefit from an expansion of low-cost childcare options, housing assistance, targeted labor market support to assist parents to prepare for and find work, and transfer payments to help families respond to crises and rise above the poverty line.",""],[1,"24","1","Household Transfer Payments for Crisis Response","Low-income families with children, especially single-parent households, could benefit from an expansion of low-cost childcare options, targeted labor market support to assist parents to prepare for and find work, and transfer payments to help families respond to crises and rise above the poverty line.",""],[1,"24","2","Home Building and Household Furnishing Assistance","Low-income families could benefit from increased access to assistance for home building and to furnish and equip homes, particularly in rural states.",""],[1,"24","3","Family Violence Victim Support Services","Victims of family violence, most but not all of whom are women, may need additional support through case management services, access to temporary housing, and access to labor market services.",""],[1,"24","4","COVID-19 Resilience Support Project","In 2020 ADB funded a project to improve the capabilities of poor and vulnerable households to withstand further impacts of COVID-19, from 2021 to 2024.",""],[1,"24","4","Welfare Support for At-Risk Elderly and Persons with Disabilities","This consists of (i) welfare support to highly at-risk elderly and persons with disabilities;",""],[1,"24","4","Food Security and Income Support for Small-Scale Producers","This consists of (ii) food security and income- generating support for small-scale agricultural producers;",""],[1,"24","4","Multidisciplinary Response to Family and Gender-Based Violence","and (iii) multidisciplinary responses to address family and gender-based violence.",""],[1,"24","5","Social Protection Policy Development and Institutional Mandate Reform","Reflecting on the experience of the COVID-19 pandemic, the government may wish to prioritize actions to address these structural and policy gaps in social protection during the plan period.",""],[1,"24","11","Child Subsidy for Eligible Low-Income Families","legislation enacted in 2023 provides funding for a $100 per month child subsidy for eligible families.",""],[1,"26","1","Low-Cost Childcare Expansion","these families could benefit from an expansion of low-cost childcare options",""],[1,"26","1","Housing Assistance for Families","these families could benefit from an expansion of low-cost childcare options, housing assistance, targeted labor market support to assist parents to prepare for and find work, and transfer payments to help families respond to crises and rise above the poverty line.",""],[1,"26","1","Family Transfer Payments","these families could benefit from an expansion of low-cost childcare options, housing assistance, targeted labor market support to assist parents to prepare for and find work, and transfer payments to help families respond to crises and rise above the poverty line.",""],[1,"30","10","Government Social Protection Gap-Filling Initiatives","There will be an increasing need to supplement the cultural system with government initiatives to fill gaps in social protection and fulfill the objective of lifting vulnerable persons above the national basic needs poverty line.",""],[1,"30","15","Housing Assistance Programme","Provide housing assistance.",""],[1,"58","9","Social Protection Framework Development","Programs to renew the quality of education, resolve NCDs and mental health disorders, and build the social protection framework supported by new social, land, and labor policies.",""]],"81":[[1,"21","1","Gender Mainstreaming Policy Implementation","The Palau National Gender Mainstreaming Policy is a key policy document that calls for the integration of gender considerations into policies and programs (footnote 22).",""],[1,"21","3","Gender Mainstreaming Accountability and Monitoring Mechanism","The Palau National Gender Mainstreaming Policy advocates for an accountability mechanism supported by the production of sex-disaggregated data and gender indicators that can be used to monitor the impacts of programs and services on women and men and to use in closing gender gaps when appropriate.",""],[1,"21","4","Disaggregated Gender Data Collection","Disaggregated gender data collection remains critical, as that would highlight the different experiences and conditions for men and women and would help policymakers craft responses that would benefit both men and women.",""]],"82":[[1,"26","6","National Policy on Aging Development Task Force","legislation enacted in January 2020 (RPPL 10-51, National Policy on Care for the Aging) created a task force to develop a National Policy on Aging",""],[1,"26","6","Social Service and Care Center for the Aged","and a plan for a Social Service and Care Center for the Aged to include permanent and temporary accommodations for older persons in need of housing.",""],[1,"26","7","National Policy on Older Persons","In response to the OEK directive, MHHS working with the World Health Organization, community stakeholders, and older persons themselves has developed a National Policy on","MHHS | the World Health Organization | community stakeholders | older persons themselves"],[1,"27","8","Age-Friendly Physical Environment Development","Create age-friendly physical environments through,",""],[1,"27","10","Non-Driving Transportation Options for Older Persons","Transportation options that do not rely on driving to ensure that older persons remain independent and mobile.",""],[1,"27","16","Geriatric and Gerontology Workforce Strengthening","Strengthening the geriatric and gerontology workforce to improve the quality of care,",""],[1,"27","17","Primary Health Care Alignment for an Aging Population","Align primary health care to respond to an aging population,",""],[1,"27","18","Healthy Aging Stakeholder Collaboration","Collaborate with public, private, and community stakeholders in support of healthy aging.",""],[1,"27","19","Senior Lunch Program Expansion","expansion of the existing senior lunch program that serves only Koror to rural communities by partnering with the school lunch program (target date, FY 2025)",""],[1,"27","19","Senior Transportation Services for Medical Appointments","develop transportation services for seniors living in Babeldaob for medical appointments and other essential tasks",""],[1,"27","19","Home Visitation Services for Older Persons","expansion of home visitation by health workers to aged persons (initiated in FY 2023)",""],[1,"27","19","Hospital Transition Unit for Seniors","operationalize the transition unit at the hospital for seniors who need continuous care (target, summer of FY 2023)",""]],"83":[[1,"28","12","National Youth Action Plan","The policy is supported by a detailed National Youth Action Plan, which sets out concrete actions to be taken by each sector and agency, along with a framework for monitoring progress toward policy objectives.",""],[1,"29","3","Youth Violence Prevention and Support Services","youth are safe from all forms of violence, abuse, neglect, and exploitation, through robust processes and comprehensive services to support youth who are at risk or who have experienced violence, and supportive families and communities encourage help-seeking",""],[1,"29","3","Youth Rehabilitation Services and Facilities","youth in conflict with the law have access to services and facilities to support their rehabilitation",""],[1,"29","5","Youth Civic Participation and Engagement Support","All youth have the knowledge, skills, forums, opportunities, and support to meaningfully participate in political decision-making and develop and participate in actions and initiatives to address climate change and environmental issues, sports, and cultural and arts programs.",""]],"84":[[1,"29","17","Climate-Proofing and Relocation of Health Facilities","The National Infrastructure and Investment Plan41 identifies a need for new investment in climate-proofing health facilities with a priority for the relocation of the national hospital and certain low-lying community health centers.",""],[1,"29","17","School Relocation, Consolidation, and Renovation Programme","Likewise, the Ministry of Education has identified new investments needed to relocate low-lying schools, consolidate inefficient small schools in Babeldaob, and renovate schools in Koror.","Ministry of Education"],[1,"30","7","Relocation of Health Facilities to Higher Ground","There is a need to relocate the national hospital and several community health centers in low-lying areas to higher ground to ensure the long-term sustainability of services.",""],[1,"30","9","Climate-Resilient Education Infrastructure Investment","There is also a need to invest in new education infrastructure to counter the effects of climate change and increase efficiencies in school management.",""],[1,"30","2","Public Land Housing Subdivision Investment","The immediate priority to meet the needs of the most vulnerable, while also building a sense of community, is to invest in housing subdivisions on public lands.",""],[1,"30","2","Rural Settlement Infrastructure and Community Amenities Upgrade","Investment into subdivision and engineering design, infrastructure (roads, power, water, sewer, storm drainage, waste management, etc.), community amenities (parks, community centers, sidewalks), and safety features (e.g., streetlights) is the most pressing immediate priority for communities outside of Koror.",""],[1,"30","13","Rural and Outer Island Population Retention and Return Housing Support","Grow the population of rural and outer island communities by actively recruiting and encouraging Palauans to move \"home\" by streamlining the housing subdivision process, easing the burden of building a home, and increasing the amount and diversity of subdivision lots and affordable homes available.",""],[1,"37","2","Climate-Proof Construction for Built Environment","Improved access to safe water supplies, improved sanitation programs and sustainable, climate-proof construction will help protect community health and the environment.",""],[1,"38","4","Controlled Migration to Upland Housing Subdivisions","Many of Palau's communities live in low-lying areas, and thus controlled migration to upland housing subdivisions is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"38","4","Climate-Resilient Engineering Design Support","To reduce the impacts of development under future climate change scenarios, engineering designs that minimize risks of subdivisions and other developments are needed, but State governments and communities have limited access to technical expertise.",""],[1,"38","4","Technical Planning and Analytical Expertise Expansion","Increasing access to technical planning and analytical expertise is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"38","5","Elevation, Reconstruction, and Rehabilitation of At-Risk Infrastructure","Elevation, reconstruction, or rehabilitation of these at-risk investments is a medium- to long-term priority.",""],[1,"38","5","Outer Islands Critical Infrastructure Improvement","in outer islands, improving key infrastructure such as water systems, transportation, safety systems, and communications is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"38","5","Solar Systems Installation and Building Code Development","Reducing disaster risk through the installation of solar systems and the development of building codes is a long-term priority.",""],[1,"39","1","Climate-Proofing Infrastructure","prioritized several short- and medium-term actions to reduce vulnerabilities, such as upland agriculture, diversification of food production, diversification of employment opportunities, and climate-proofing infrastructure.",""],[1,"39","3","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Investment","Improve future climate resilience in the existing stock and future investments in infrastructure.",""],[1,"39","12","Climate-Proof Construction Initiative","Improved access to safe water supplies, improved sanitation programs and sustainable, climate-proof construction will help protect community health and the environment.",""],[1,"58","21","Climate-Proof Public Water Systems Upgrade and Expansion","Improve, expand, and build new climate-proof Public Water Systems.",""],[1,"59","1","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Adaptation","Adapt infrastructure for climate change.",""]],"85":[[1,"30","14","Community Design and Neighborhood Planning Support","Strengthen a sense of place by conducting community design and planning and offering support services to create neighborhoods that include increasing access to goods and services, a growing number of childcare options, recreational opportunities, and community educational programming.",""],[1,"32","5","Land Use Planning, Zoning, and Mitigation Measures","Improved governance capacities are also a priority to ensure that economic growth and other forms of development respect Palauan culture, including land use planning, zoning, and mitigation, and policies that limit the impacts of foreign labor on uniquely Palauan communities.",""],[1,"35","1","Land Use Master Plan Development Assistance","need assistance in developing land use master plans that allow for climate change and social and economic development.",""],[1,"35","5","State Master Plan Development and Update","The development or update of most States' master plans is ongoing through the GEF 6 project, led by the Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries, and the Environment.","Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries, and the Environment"],[1,"37","2","Sustainable Land Use Planning and Building Code Enforcement","Sustainable Land Management principles are key, including land use planning and building codes, to minimize the impacts of pollution and habitat loss.",""],[1,"38","3","Land Use Plan and Zoning Implementation","Implementation of land use plans and zoning, via mandated Planning Commissions and State Planning Offices, is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"39","5","Master Plan and Sustainable Land Use Planning Support","The States need additional assistance in developing master plans and sustainable land use plans that allow for climate change and social and economic development.",""],[1,"43","1","State Master Plan Implementation Support","An immediate priority is to enable the implementation of State Master Plans, which include economic development objectives, climate resiliency objectives, and collective benefit principles, through the creation of new positions for State Planners60 which can coordinate, implement, and track master plans.",""],[1,"43","1","State Planning Commission Support and Participation Mechanism","Achieving participatory input and buy-in from a supported and funded State Planning Commission is another immediate priority.",""],[1,"55","7","State Planning Capacity and Commission Support","Hiring state planners and funding state planning commissions is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"55","7","Inclusive Planning Commission Participation","Empowering representation and participation, particularly from traditional leaders and community groups, through planning commissions is another immediate priority.",""],[1,"55","7","Multi-State Spatial and Land Planning Technical Support","Ensuring multi-state spatial and land planning technical support",""],[1,"56","1","Spatial Data Support and Regional Planning Assistance","services, such as spatial data support as provided by PALARIS79 and regional and cross-border planning, is another immediate priority.",""],[1,"56","1","State Planner and Regional Planning Body Technical Assistance","Building on partnerships between state governments and the national government, as well as between communities and NGO partners, remains a priority that can be achieved through dedicated state planners and regional planning bodies, and associated technical assistance.",""],[1,"56","2","State Government Technical Assistance Capacity Support","This can be accomplished by financing and enabling access to technical assistance in engineering, planning, financial analysis, Environmental Impact Statements, CIP planning, and scenario planning.",""],[1,"56","3","Empower Representative Planning Commissions","empowering representative planning commissions is an immediate priority",""],[1,"56","3","Strengthen Traditional and Elected Leader Engagement Forums","Communities want to strengthen ties between traditional and elected leaders and engage traditional leaders more deeply in governance, by providing forums and decision-point opportunities",""],[1,"56","3","Construct New Modern State Offices","Building new, modern state offices is a long-term priority for some communities",""],[1,"56","8","Palau Automated Land and Resource Information System","The Palau Automated Land and Resource Information System, Bureau of Budget and Planning, Ministry of Finance.","Bureau of Budget and Planning, Ministry of Finance"],[1,"57","8","New Land Policy","A new land policy could facilitate private investment and economic development as well as urban development planning and help to further protect Palauan ownership.",""],[1,"58","1","State Planner Recruitment and Planning Commission Empowerment","State planners need to be hired and representative and participatory planning commissions empowered and resourced to implement state master plans, land use plans, and zoning codes.",""],[1,"58","2","Regional Planning Services Strengthening","Multi-state, cross-border, and state-to-national coordination should be strengthened by providing regional planning services (via a central planning office under PNCA 31).",""],[1,"58","3","Long-term Support for PALARIS-Based Communities","Multi-state and spatial planning needs support by securing long-term assistance for communities based at PALARIS.",""],[1,"58","4","Technical Expertise Support for Community Needs","Access to technical expertise in engineering, planning, financial analysis, Environmental Impact Statements, CIP planning, and scenario planning should be provided through annual financing, or the provision of personnel dedicated to community needs.",""],[1,"59","13","Master and Land Use Plan Implementation and Coordination","Enable, implement, and coordinate Master and Land Use Plans, Zoning, and CIP.",""],[1,"60","5","Strengthened Policy, Spatial, and Budgetary Planning","the country overview and the communities share a common concern to improve policy, spatial, and budgetary planning.",""],[1,"60","5","Technical Planning and Engineering Support for Rural and Outer Islands","For the rural and outer island communities, this concern stretches to the need for strengthened technical planning, engineering, and analysis.",""]],"86":[[1,"33","19","Palau National Environmental Management Strategy 2022-2030","A desire to better coordinate and prioritize across sectors triggered the development of the 2022 - 2030 Palau National Environmental Management Strategy (NEMS)46.",""],[1,"35","3","Integrated Land Management and Sustainable Land Use Planning","Thus, land management in Palau is considered in two categories: 1) Protected areas and 2) Sustainable Land Management (SLM) for all other lands.",""],[1,"35","4","Marine Resource Research, Monitoring, and Spatial Planning","Research, monitoring, and spatial planning, sustainable management of coastal fisheries, growth of aquaculture, expansion of protected areas, more sustainable tourism, and management of diverse habitats will",""],[1,"35","4","Sustainable Coastal Fisheries Management","Research, monitoring, and spatial planning, sustainable management of coastal fisheries, growth of aquaculture, expansion of protected areas, more sustainable tourism, and management of diverse habitats will",""],[1,"39","7","Sustainable Coastal Fisheries Management","Research, monitoring, and spatial planning, sustainable management of coastal fisheries, growth of aquaculture, expansion of protected areas, more sustainable tourism, and management of diverse habitats will help to preserve and sustainably use marine environments.",""],[1,"35","4","Aquaculture Expansion and Protected Area Management","Research, monitoring, and spatial planning, sustainable management of coastal fisheries, growth of aquaculture, expansion of protected areas, more sustainable tourism, and management of diverse habitats will",""],[1,"36","2","Palau National Marine Sanctuary Regulation and Zoning","The entire EEZ is regulated under the Palau National Marine Sanctuary (PNMS) Act, which established a Domestic Fishing Zone, a closed Marine Protected Area, and an Artisanal Fishing Zone; the act also reconfirmed each State Government's territorial rights from shoreline to 12 nautical miles.",""],[1,"36","2","Sustainable Domestic Pelagic Fishing Support","Support for sustainable domestic pelagic fishing, improved security and enforcement, and expansion of benefit-sharing will protect offshore marine resources.",""],[1,"39","8","Sustainable Domestic Pelagic Fishing Support","Support for increased sustainable domestic pelagic fishing, improved security and enforcement, and expansion of benefit-sharing will protect offshore marine resources.",""],[1,"36","3","Catchment Management and Watershed Protection","Catchment management and protection, freshwater monitoring and supply management, and freshwater lake and estuarine habitat protection will help to preserve Palau's freshwater environment.",""],[1,"36","3","Freshwater Monitoring and Supply Management","Catchment management and protection, freshwater monitoring and supply management, and freshwater lake and estuarine habitat protection will help to preserve Palau's freshwater environment.",""],[1,"39","9","Freshwater Monitoring and Supply Management","Freshwater catchment management and protection, freshwater monitoring and supply management, freshwater lake and estuarine habitat protection, and management of the cumulative impacts of sewage and septic tanks will help preserve the freshwater environment.",""],[1,"36","3","Freshwater Lake and Estuarine Habitat Protection","Catchment management and protection, freshwater monitoring and supply management, and freshwater lake and estuarine habitat protection will help to preserve Palau's freshwater environment.",""],[1,"39","9","Freshwater Lake and Estuarine Habitat Protection","Freshwater catchment management and protection, freshwater monitoring and supply management, freshwater lake and estuarine habitat protection, and management of the cumulative impacts of sewage and septic tanks will help preserve the freshwater environment.",""],[1,"36","4","Endangered Species Regulation","Palau's biodiversity will be better conserved by endangered species regulation, control of invasive alien species, an increasingly effective Protected Areas Network (PAN), and sustainable tourism practices.",""],[1,"39","10","Endangered Species Regulation","Biodiversity will be better conserved by endangered species regulation, control of invasive alien species, an increasingly effective PAN, and sustainable tourism practices.",""],[1,"36","4","Invasive Alien Species Control","Palau's biodiversity will be better conserved by endangered species regulation, control of invasive alien species, an increasingly effective Protected Areas Network (PAN), and sustainable tourism practices.",""],[1,"39","10","Invasive Alien Species Control","Biodiversity will be better conserved by endangered species regulation, control of invasive alien species, an increasingly effective PAN, and sustainable tourism practices.",""],[1,"36","4","Protected Areas Network Strengthening","Palau's biodiversity will be better conserved by endangered species regulation, control of invasive alien species, an increasingly effective Protected Areas Network (PAN), and sustainable tourism practices.",""],[1,"39","6","Coordinated Land Use and Terrestrial Habitat Protection","Terrestrial ecosystems and food production habitats can be better preserved through coordinated land use planning, agro-biodiverse food production, water quality and supply protection, control of key invasive alien species, and management and protection of terrestrial habitats and resources.",""],[1,"39","7","Marine Research, Monitoring, and Spatial Planning","Research, monitoring, and spatial planning, sustainable management of coastal fisheries, growth of aquaculture, expansion of protected areas, more sustainable tourism, and management of diverse habitats will help to preserve and sustainably use marine environments.",""],[1,"39","7","Aquaculture Expansion and Protected Areas Management","Research, monitoring, and spatial planning, sustainable management of coastal fisheries, growth of aquaculture, expansion of protected areas, more sustainable tourism, and management of diverse habitats will help to preserve and sustainably use marine environments.",""],[1,"39","9","Freshwater Catchment Management and Protection","Freshwater catchment management and protection, freshwater monitoring and supply management, freshwater lake and estuarine habitat protection, and management of the cumulative impacts of sewage and septic tanks will help preserve the freshwater environment.",""],[1,"39","9","Sewage and Septic Tank Impact Management","Freshwater catchment management and protection, freshwater monitoring and supply management, freshwater lake and estuarine habitat protection, and management of the cumulative impacts of sewage and septic tanks will help preserve the freshwater environment.",""],[1,"39","10","Sustainable Tourism Practices","Biodiversity will be better conserved by endangered species regulation, control of invasive alien species, an increasingly effective PAN, and sustainable tourism practices.",""],[1,"59","2","Integrated Land, Freshwater, and Marine Planning","Continue land, freshwater, and marine planning for climate change and development.",""],[1,"59","2","Erosion and Sedimentation Control and Land Cover Restoration","Institutionalize erosion and sedimentation control and restore land cover.",""],[1,"70","8","Land Rehabilitation and Invasive Species Control","Reduced area of land that is actively eroding and/or facing invasive species threats",""]],"87":[[1,"39","1","Upland Agriculture and Food Production Diversification","prioritized several short- and medium-term actions to reduce vulnerabilities, such as upland agriculture, diversification of food production, diversification of employment opportunities, and climate-proofing infrastructure.",""],[1,"39","4","Sustainable Agriculture Production Support","Support for tripling of diverse agriculture production in an environmentally and culturally sustainable manner.",""],[1,"44","3","Agriculture and Aquaculture Production Expansion","Food security needs to be increased by expanding agriculture and aquaculture production by families, communities, and businesses.",""],[1,"44","3","Food Production Diversification and Market Expansion","Diversification of food production, and expansion of the number and types of markets available should also be supported.",""],[1,"59","6","Small-Scale Agriculture and Fisheries Support Programme","Support small-scale agriculture and fisheries.",""],[1,"63","2","Farmer Training and Support Programme","Post-Covid there has been a resurgence of interest in local farming and demand for training sessions outpaces supply.",""],[1,"63","5","Livestock Breeding and Hatchery Facility Support","Production capacity and demand for livestock piglets and chicks were steadily increasing and will be supported by new facilities being constructed with the assistance of bilateral partners, but operational support in terms of extension services and facility operations is needed.",""],[1,"63","5","Piglet and Chick Production Support","The BOA supported livestock farmers through the production of piglets and chicks.",""],[1,"63","5","Cost-Based Livestock Feed Supply","BOA has a feed mill and manufactures feed which it sells to farmers at cost.",""],[1,"64","1","Seed Bank Expansion and Climate-Resilient Water Systems Investment","The seed bank needs to be extended and investment into water systems is also needed to make it climate resilient.",""],[1,"64","3","Expansion of Compost Production Facilities","Neither BOA nor Koror State can keep up with demand, and expansion of compost facilities is needed to further enhance soil quality.",""],[1,"64","4","Farmer Tilling and Equipment Rental Support","BOA offers this service to farmers at a very low cost, either by directly tilling (approximately 20 acres per year) or by renting equipment at a subsidized cost.",""],[1,"64","4","Agricultural Extension and Input Supply Expansion","The growing demand needs increased extension services, additional equipment and supplies to service a growing number of farmers on larger swaths of land.",""],[1,"64","4","Agricultural Water Storage and Irrigation Investment","Commercial farms in particular need assistance to invest in infrastructure such as water tanks and irrigation systems.",""],[1,"64","4","Agricultural Access Road Development","Many of the best soils and agriculture zones need access roads.",""],[1,"64","5","Invasive Species Control and Monitoring Programme","Persistent control is needed, as is regular research to identify new and emerging biotypes of invasive species and to keep up to date with control methods that will keep them at minimal populations.",""],[1,"64","5","Agricultural Laboratory Operational Support","BOA has a building for a laboratory but needs regular supplies to keep it operational.",""],[1,"66","3","Agricultural Capital Investment Facilities","The following major additional capital investments of (i) a post-harvest processing facility, (ii) a swine breeding facility, (iii) a poultry hatching facility, and (iv) a poultry slaughterhouse are all on track to be completed by the end of 2023.",""],[1,"66","4","Agricultural Support Services and Food Production Facilities","The Taiwan Technical Mission (TTM) works in close partnership with BOA in providing a range of support services in the fields of livestock, horticultural crops, and aquaculture.",""],[1,"66","4","Agricultural Vocational Training and Extension Programme","The Palau Community College Cooperative Research and Extension (PCC- CRE) program is part of the US Land Grant System which supports Palau's agricultural sector through its vocational training courses, an agriculture research station, and cooperative extension services.",""],[1,"67","2","Agricultural Sedimentation and Erosion Control Programme","Implementation of best practices in sedimentation and erosion control in agriculture, combined with land use planning and zoning to reduce future sedimentation is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"67","2","Erosion Control, Tree Planting, and Land Cover Rehabilitation Programme","Institutionalizing a program of erosion control, tree planting, or land cover rehabilitation (for which there is proof of concept) is also an immediate priority.",""],[1,"67","2","Sustainable Agricultural Expansion and Extension Services","Expanding food production by opening new leases on land and water is an immediate priority, and identification and extension services to ensure sustainable and culturally relevant practices, especially in traditional agro-forestry, agro-biodiversity, and taro production areas, is another immediate priority.",""],[1,"67","3","Climate-Resilient Agricultural Expansion","Thus, safe, and climate-resilient expansion of agriculture is necessary and an immediate priority.",""],[1,"67","3","Farm Water Infrastructure Support","Individual farmers need assistance, particularly with water infrastructure to increase the resilience of their farms.",""],[1,"67","3","Invasive Alien Species Management Program","Management of invasive alien species (IAS), including control of fruit flies, coconut rhinoceros beetles, and invasive vines, and prevention of new introductions such as brown tree snakes and tilapia, are important for food security.",""],[1,"67","3","Institutionalization of Invasive Alien Species Programs","Institutionalizing existing IAS programs of prevention, awareness, reporting, and control (for which there is also proof of concept) is also an immediate priority for food-productive areas.",""],[1,"67","4","Taro Patch Revitalization in Koror's Rock Islands","Revitalization of taro patches in Koror's Rock Islands is a priority for both food security and cultural protection.",""],[1,"67","4","Tabletop and Home Garden Support for Koror","Due to limited space, tabletop gardens and home gardens are the priority for Koror.",""],[1,"67","4","NGO-Supported Garden Assistance with BOA","These are supported by NGOs with assistance from BOA.",""],[1,"68","2","Farm Loan Program","The National Development Bank of Palau provides lending to agriculture including a Farm Loan Program, but few loans have been approved",""],[1,"68","9","Farmer Training and Commercialization Support","The BOA with other partner agencies is training and encouraging farmers to increase production and commercialize farming operations",""],[1,"69","2","Agriculture and Food System Planning and Coordination","Comprehensive agriculture and food system planning and coordination and a comprehensive local food production and consumption campaign",""],[1,"69","3","Agricultural Extension and Support Services Expansion","Expansion of agricultural extension and support services in livestock, fruit, and vegetables",""],[1,"69","4","Climate-Resilient Sustainable Community Farming Expansion","Expansion of climate-resilient and culturally and environmentally sustainable farms in communities and increasing production of root crops, vegetables, fruit, and livestock",""],[1,"69","10","Nursery and Compost Facilities Expansion","Expansion of nursery and compost facilities",""],[1,"70","5","Local Food Production Expansion","Doubled local food production to improve food security (accessibility, affordability, and availability) of locally produced livestock, root crops, vegetables, and fruits, with a minimal negative impact on the environment or culture",""],[1,"70","8","Comprehensive Food Systems Policy","Comprehensive Food Systems Policy in place",""],[1,"70","8","Livestock and Poultry Production Expansion","Double livestock piglet and chick production (2022-2026)",""],[1,"70","8","Seed Bank and Seedling Production Expansion","7,500 square meters of seed bank operational",""],[1,"70","8","Compost Production Expansion","Doubled production of compost (500m3 in 2023 to 1,000m3 facility)",""],[1,"70","8","Land Tillage and Cropland Expansion","Increase land tillage per year by 25%: From 20 acres tilled per year in 2022 to 25 acres tilled per year in FY2027 to 100 acres of new cropland in 4 years.",""],[1,"70","8","Fruit Sapling Production and Fruit Fly Control","Increase fruit sapling production by 33%: From 1500 fruit trees/hedge species saplings in 2022 to 2,000/year; Decrease fruit fly damage on at least 50 fruit farms.",""],[1,"70","8","Farmer and Food Processor Training Programme","400 trained farmers/food processors (At least 4 training per year targeting 100 farmers per year)",""],[1,"70","8","State Partnership Network for Local Food Systems","16 State partnerships to produce, consume, or sell local foods (new agriculture zones, construction of markets, construction of roads/water, rehabilitation of productive landscapes, etc.)",""],[1,"70","28","Nursery and Greenhouse Expansion with Rainwater Harvesting System","Expand nursery/greenhouse and rainwater harvesting system",""]],"88":[[1,"43","3","Tourism Product Diversification and Community Marketing Initiative","Expanding the number, diversity, and quality of cultural and natural tourism products, equitably marketing tourism products in all communities, and increasing the number of local Palauans able to participate in and benefit from the tourism industry is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"43","3","Rural Tourism Accommodation and Support Services Expansion","Increasing the stock of small tourism accommodations, restaurants, and support services is a medium- to long-term priority in rural communities.",""],[1,"43","4","Tourism Product and Accommodation Expansion","expanding tourism products, accommodations of all types, restaurants, and support services are immediate priorities.",""],[1,"44","4","Cultural and Natural Tourism Product Expansion and Promotion","The number, diversity, and quality of cultural and natural tourism products should be expanded and promoted,",""],[1,"44","4","Local Tourism Training Programme","an increasing number of Palauans need to be trained in local tourism, including tourism business management, arts and handicrafts, and customer relations.",""],[1,"59","8","Tourism Product Development, Promotion, and Training Programme","Increase tourism products, expand promotion, and train Palauans in tourism.",""],[1,"60","4","Tourism Product and Skills Development","The communities also specifically prioritize support for small businesses and for more tourism products and skills in tourism.",""]],"89":[[1,"42","6","Fiscal Revenue Recovery and Public Enterprise Reform","the economic growth strategy will be complemented by the recovery and expansion of government revenues through continued fiscal discipline, more efficient revenue collection, and SOE, social security, and pension reforms to reduce if not eliminate demands for government subsidies and transfers to public sector financial institutions.",""],[1,"42","6","Elimination of Subsidies to Palau Public Utilities Corporation","The IMF has estimated that eliminating subsidies to the Palau Public Utilities Corporation (PPUC) over the next 5 years would yield a cumulative saving of 1 percent of GDP.",""],[1,"42","6","Staged Introduction of Full Cost Recovery Tariffs for Water and Wastewater","The greatest fiscal risks facing the nation are failing to adopt a staged introduction of full cost recovery tariffs in water and wastewater and collapse in either the Social Security or Civil Service Pension Plan, which on current trends are projected to collapse within the next 10 years.",""],[1,"42","6","Social Security and Civil Service Pension Plan Reform","The greatest fiscal risks facing the nation are failing to adopt a staged introduction of full cost recovery tariffs in water and wastewater and collapse in either the Social Security or Civil Service Pension Plan, which on current trends are projected to collapse within the next 10 years.",""],[1,"42","7","Fiscal Reform Package","The government continues to implement fiscal reforms including the adoption of a Fiscal Responsibility Framework in 2018, a business profits tax in 2022, the introduction of a goods and services tax in January 2023 (a value-added tax), reforms to the wages and hotel occupancy taxes, and reforms to revenue administration.",""],[1,"43","7","Prudent Fiscal Policy and Revenue Mobilization Reform","the economic growth strategy will be complemented by the recovery and expansion of government revenues through continued prudent fiscal policy, more efficient revenue collection, and SOE, social security, and pension reforms to reduce if not eliminate demands for government subsidies.",""],[1,"46","3","State Expenditure Efficiency Technical Support","Continued funding by the National Government budget process, and continued access to technical services to improve the efficiency of State expenditures, is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"46","3","National-State Planning and Budget Alignment","An important challenge for all the states is the need to strengthen planning and align national and state development objectives and budgets.",""],[1,"47","2","State-Owned Enterprise Governance Policy and Bill","The President issued an SOE policy in 2014 which focused on the future legal, regulatory, and governance arrangements.",""],[1,"47","2","State-Owned Enterprise Performance and CSO Oversight Measures","A set of policy principles were outlined to support the primary objective, the specification of community service obligations (CSOs).",""],[1,"47","2","PPUC Operational and Regulatory Reforms","PPUC underwent a series of operational and regulatory reforms in 2020-2021 linked to an ADB policy- based loan.66",""],[1,"47","3","SOE Policy Legal Embedding and Mandate Reform","The Ministry of Finance intends to embed the policy in its enabling legislation RPPL 9-4, and this will provide the Ministry with the authority to mandate SOE policies.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"47","3","PPUC Pilot for SOE Initiatives","To further progress SOE initiatives, the Ministry of Finance will employ the PPUC as a pilot.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"47","3","SOE Board Nomination Procedure Reform","Additionally, there is a need for a new board nomination procedure to ensure that the SOE sector operates with qualified directors who possess the necessary skills and experience to effectively oversee the operations of these entities.",""],[1,"53","8","Public Finance Management Roadmap","The PEFA will be followed by the preparation of a Public Finance Management roadmap to be implemented by the government over the period of the PDP.",""],[1,"54","1","Fiscal Responsibility and Debt Management Reform","The government recently approved a Fiscal Responsibility Act (18 November 2021) that incorporates debt management policies and strategies, approved the External Debt Management Act (signed into law on 18 November 2021) and established a Public Debt Management Unit (effective April 2022), approved a comprehensive tax reform package (signed into law on 29 September 2021), and operationalized a National Infrastructure Investment Plan, 2021 to 2030.","Ministry of Finance (MOF)"],[1,"54","1","Economic and Fiscal Reporting and Medium-Term Fiscal Strategy Guidelines","The Ministry of Finance (MOF) also started to produce Economic and Fiscal Updates to underpin the budget and operationalized Medium-Term Fiscal Strategy Guidelines (29 June 2022).","Ministry of Finance (MOF)"],[1,"54","1","Social Security Reform Bill Preparation","The government has also supported the preparation of a social security reform bill.",""],[1,"54","1","Public Finance Management Strengthening Support","ADB and PFTAC are assisting the government to strengthen its public finance management.",""],[1,"54","2","Defined Contribution Pension Reform","finalize pension reform by switching to a Defined Contribution Plan by FY 24",""],[1,"54","2","Internal Auditor and Controller General Position Creation","create a position for an Internal Auditor/ Controller General",""],[1,"54","2","Tax Administration Facility Construction","construct a tax building in Babeldaob near the capitol building in FY 25",""],[1,"54","2","Customs and Immigration Facilities and Systems Upgrade","construct a new main facility for customs and immigration in Malakal at a cost of $2 million, to construct additional customs and immigration offices in Babeldaob, Peleliu and Angaur, and to further strengthen ASYCUDA and immigration information systems over the period of the PDP",""],[1,"54","2","Debt Management System Establishment","establish a debt management system in FY24 costing an estimated $3 million",""],[1,"54","3","State Public Finance Management SOP Development and Adoption","One of the successful diagnostic tools identified is the development and adoption of the state government's public finance management standard operating procedures (PFM SOP) to enhance capacities surrounding management, documentation, and reporting of fiscal and public assets and resources towards consistent and sustainable delivery of public goods and services.","Ministry of State"],[1,"57","11","Technical Assistance for State Government Finance Management","Further technical assistance would help strengthen the management of State government finances.",""],[1,"59","7","Public Finance Reform","Continue to reform all public finances to stem losses, raise revenues, reduce debt, and coordinate aid.",""]],"90":[[1,"51","7","E-Government Expansion Support","MOF plans to further support the expansion of e- government","MOF"],[1,"51","7","Bureau Assessment and Certification Programme","establish an assessment and certification program for each of the bureaus under the Ministry of Finance","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"51","7","Government Staff Ethics Training and Certification Programme","to establish a program for ethical training and certification of government staff",""],[1,"53","7","Public Sector Modernization Program","A long-term program in support of the modernization of the public sector will be needed to continue to assess the system, ensure that HR management is consistent across all Ministries, continue management training, and assess the need for new legislation.","Ministry of Human Resources (HR), Culture, Tourism, and Development | Ministry of Finance"],[1,"57","10","Public Sector Modernization Program","A long-term program in support of public sector modernization would help improve public sector productivity.",""],[1,"54","3","Local Governance Strengthening Project","The joint pilot partnership, the Local Governance Strengthening Project (LGSP), has provided the space for collaborative work between the MOF, Office of the Public Auditor, five pilot states, and the Ministry of State to engage within the local government sector to identify gaps and to develop diagnostic tools to strengthen local governance.","Ministry of State | MOF | Office of the Public Auditor"],[1,"54","3","Public Participation and Civic Responsibility Awareness Initiative","In addition, increased public participation and engagement in policy development through increasing public awareness of the individual and collective civic responsibility prescribed by the Palau Constitution as well as their respective state government Constitutions.","Ministry of State"],[1,"54","4","Expansion of Local Governance Diagnostic Tools","The Ministry of State has utilized the joint pilot partnership towards developing content and contextualized diagnostic tools to strengthen local governance at the state government level and is now seeking the resources to expand and extend the diagnostic tools to benefit the remaining eleven state governments outside of the LGSP.","Ministry of State"],[1,"55","4","Permanent Government Policy Planning Institution","A permanent institution of central and state government policy planning is therefore needed to ensure that national and sector plan priorities are identified for funding and to facilitate the coordination and formulation of new policies in support of growth and development.",""],[1,"55","5","Central Economic Planning Office and Aid Coordination Office","MOF plans to establish a central economic planning office that will include an Aid Coordination Office and be responsible for the continued assessment of macroeconomic performance, the strengthened assessment of all sector development, and the assessment of economic feasibility including recurrent cost implications of all investment projects, proposed PPPs, and other capital expenditure including that of the SOEs.",""],[1,"56","4","Central Statistical Data Collection Point","The government has adopted a policy not to burden the private sector with requests for statistics but to adopt a central collection point for each of the major economic categories of information.",""],[1,"56","4","Strengthening General Government Financial Reporting Capacity","Strengthening the capacity of state governments and other units of the general government to provide timely and adequate financial statements would support the compilation of fiscal data at the general government level.",""],[1,"56","5","National Statistical Data Collection and Development Programme","The Office of Budget and Planning will continue to conduct a population census every ten years, a household income and expenditure survey every 5 years, and develop a series of quarterly economic statistics.","Office of Budget and Planning"],[1,"57","4","National Development Planning Structure Reform","The Office of the President is developing a new structure for national development planning.",""],[1,"57","6","Donor and Development Partner Coordination Mechanism","Donor and development partner development programs could be better coordinated in the interest of Palau's development.",""],[1,"59","12","Public Sector Productivity Improvement Strategy","Design and implement strategies to improve public sector productivity.",""],[1,"59","16","Participatory Planning and Government-Wide Policy Formulation","Adopt participatory planning and strengthen government-wide public policy formulation.",""],[1,"59","16","National Unity Programs","Programs to unify Palau.",""],[1,"59","16","Aid Coordination Improvement","Better coordinate aid.",""],[1,"59","17","Technical Planning and Engineering Expertise Support","Stabilize and increase access to technical planning, engineering, and analytical expertise.",""],[1,"45","1","Community Outreach Expansion Program","MOF has a program to expand community outreach.","MOF"],[1,"45","4","Annual State Block Grant Transfers","The national government provides annual state block grants to each of the 16 states for operational and capital improvement projects.",""],[1,"57","12","Permanent Central Government Policy Planning Institution","A permanent institution of central government policy planning will help facilitate the formulation of new policies in support of growth and development.",""]],"91":[[1,"51","6","Increase Police Presence in Outer Islands","an immediate need is to increase police presence, or expand the enforcement capacity of Rangers, to deter such crimes.",""],[1,"51","6","Expand Ranger Enforcement Capacity","an immediate need is to increase police presence, or expand the enforcement capacity of Rangers, to deter such crimes.",""],[1,"58","6","Strengthening Police Presence and Ranger Enforcement Capacity","The police presence (through MOJ and/or local deputies) and enforcement capacity of Rangers need to be strengthened in all communities.",""],[1,"59","20","Police Presence and Ranger Enforcement Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen police presence and increase Ranger enforcement capacity.",""],[1,"60","5","Public Safety and Information Access Improvements","The urban communities and the outer islands are also concerned with public safety and better access to information.",""]],"92":[[1,"58","9","Education Quality Renewal Program","Programs to renew the quality of education, resolve NCDs and mental health disorders, and build the social protection framework supported by new social, land, and labor policies.",""],[1,"71","2","Palau Head Start Early Childhood Education Programme","Early childhood education (ages 3-5) is provided by Palau Head Start, a program of the non-profit, Palau Community Action Agency.",""],[1,"71","2","Public Primary and Secondary Education Provision","Primary and secondary education (K-12) is provided by the Ministry of Education.","Ministry of Education"],[1,"71","2","On-Island Tertiary Education Provision","Tertiary education on-island is provided by Palau Community College (PCC) while the Palau Scholarship Board provides financial support to students who meet support criteria who are pursuing tertiary education off-island.",""],[1,"71","3","Head Start Early Childhood Education Program","The Head Start program has provided early childhood education in Palau for 56 years.",""],[1,"71","6","Elementary School Consolidation Plan","Consequently, the MOE consolidated three elementary schools in eastern Babeldaob into one school in 2011 and plans to consolidate the remaining six public elementary schools in northern and western Babeldaob into two schools.","MOE"],[1,"71","7","Universal and Mandatory Kindergarten for 5-Year-Olds","It will become universal and mandatory for 5-year-olds in SY2023-2024.",""],[1,"72","1","Relocation of Elementary Schools to Higher Ground","also address the need to relocate three of these elementary schools to higher ground because of climate change and sea level rise.",""],[1,"72","3","National Scholarship Administration and Higher Education Scholarship Support","The Palau National Scholarship Board (PNSB) was established-to provide scholarships to Palauan citizens pursuing higher education in colleges and universities abroad taking into consideration the national objectives and priorities of the Republic of Palau.",""],[1,"72","4","Harmonization of Head Start with Ministry of Education Schooling Arrangements","Key issues are harmonizing Head Start with the Ministry of Education specific to year-round schooling and mandatory kindergarten for 5-years olds scheduled to begin in SY2023-2024.","Ministry of Education"],[1,"72","7","Online Learning Programs","Establishing online learning programs",""],[1,"72","8","Teacher Professional Development and Continuing Education","Supporting teacher professional development and continuing education",""],[1,"72","9","School Curriculum Review and Update","· Reviewing and updating the school curriculum",""],[1,"72","10","Year-Round School Year Implementation","Implementing year-round school year",""],[1,"72","11","Automated Student Information System","Implementing an automated Student Information System",""],[1,"72","12","Public School Accreditation through WASC","Accrediting all public schools through the Western Association of Schools and Colleges (WASC)",""],[1,"72","13","WICHE Membership Acquisition","Gaining membership of the Western Interstate Commission for Higher Education (WICHE)",""],[1,"72","14","Special Education, Adult Education, and Career and Technical Education Programs","Implementing special education, adult education, and career and technical education programs with federal funding support",""],[1,"72","15","Daily Student Transport and Meal Support","Providing daily student busing, breakfast, and lunch",""],[1,"72","16","School Facilities Upgrading","Upgrading school facilities",""],[1,"73","1","Student Recruitment and Scholarship Support for Regional Enrollment","PCC is exploring options for attracting more students from the Federated States of Micronesia (FSM) and the Republic of the Marshall Islands (RMI) by providing travel scholarships, financial aid packages, and a rich educational and cultural experience.",""],[1,"73","1","Online and Hybrid Degree Programme Expansion","PCC is also exploring options to support online or hybrid bachelor's and master's degree programs that will boost enrollment, strengthen partnerships with U.S. Institutions of Higher Education, and deliver a more diverse range of educational opportunities to Palauans.",""],[1,"73","2","Post-Secondary Scholarship Support and Outreach Programme","PNSB undertakes initiatives to help Palauan students enroll and succeed in post-secondary studies.",""],[1,"73","2","Paid Summer Internship for Returning Graduates","To encourage students to return to Palau on graduation, PNSB has introduced a paid summer internship open to students in their sophomore and junior years of college with the intent of familiarizing them with career opportunities at home.",""],[1,"73","4","Establishment of a K-12 Public School in Babeldaob","an executive order issued by the Office of the President creating a task force to initiate work on establishing a K-12 public school in Babeldaob.",""],[1,"74","1","Early Head Start Community Assessment","Head Start is undertaking a community assessment to guide future directions including the level of community support for Early Head Start.",""],[1,"74","1","Basic Education System Improvement and Reform","For grades 1-12, the Ministry of Education intends to improve the appropriateness, staffing, management, learning environment, technology integration, monitoring, and overall productivity of education by increasing investment and exploring areas for systemic reforms and transformation.","Ministry of Education"],[1,"74","1","Tertiary Staff Compensation and Enrollment Expansion","For tertiary education, PCC plans to increase salaries and benefits paid to highly qualified staff and increase student enrollment by positioning itself as the tertiary institution of choice for students from the FSM and RMI.",""],[1,"74","1","Post-Secondary Preparation and Return Incentive Support","The PNSB will continue to encourage and support students in preparing for post- secondary education abroad while incentivizing their return to Palau upon graduation.",""],[1,"74","2","Early Head Start Programme","Introduce Early Head Start to provide early learning for children aged 1-2 years.",""]],"93":[[1,"74","3","Recurrent Education Sector Operating Expenditure","Continued recurrent expenditure of $9.4 million per annum to fund teachers, administration, and other staffing, staff running costs, school and headquarter running costs, maintenance, and repairs.",""],[1,"74","4","Curriculum Review and Revision","Conduct curriculum review and revision.",""],[1,"74","5","Palauan Studies Strengthening Programme","Strengthen Palauan studies (teaching of history, values, language, and culture).",""],[1,"74","6","Financial Literacy Integration Across Curriculum","Integrate financial literacy across all content areas.",""],[1,"74","7","Parental Engagement Program Formalization","Formalize parental engagement program.",""],[1,"74","8","Performance Metrics and Reporting Guidelines","Develop performance metrics and reporting guidelines.",""],[1,"74","15","School Leadership Training Program","Establish a school leadership training program.",""],[1,"74","16","Expanded Learning Pathways and Advanced Placement Option","Increase learning pathways including the introduction of an Advance Placement option.",""],[1,"74","17","Instructional Strategies Improvement","Improve instructional strategies to meet the needs of diverse learners.",""],[1,"75","5","Inclusive and Quality Education and Training Services","Grades 1-12: Inclusive and quality education and training services are provided for all students",""],[1,"75","8","Parent Engagement and School Leadership Partnership Mechanism","Strengthen MOE and parental partnerships as measured using parent portals for student grades, monthly parent meetings with MOE leadership, and resulting survey results.","MOE"],[1,"75","8","Technology-Enabled Curriculum Improvement","Improve educational curriculum by utilizing technology to enable more individualized instruction in all academic core classes in all grade levels.",""],[1,"75","8","CAL Implementation in English and Math","Implement the systems of CAL in all English and Math classes in all grades from K-12.",""],[1,"75","8","Early Head Start Expansion","Early Head Start will serve children 1-2 years old.",""],[1,"75","35","Head Start Federal Funding Eligibility","Palau will continue to be eligible for Head Start Federal funds under new compact.",""]],"94":[[1,"74","9","School Consolidation Review","Explore school consolidation.",""],[1,"74","10","School Facilities Upgrade Programme","Upgrade school facilities including repair and replacement of buildings.",""],[1,"75","8","School Rehabilitation and Replacement Programme","School buildings are repaired or replaced to provide an optimum learning environment.",""],[1,"75","8","Elementary School Construction and Consolidation Project","By 2026 construct 4 new elementary schools to consolidate and replace 8 existing elementary schools on Babeldaob.",""],[1,"75","8","School Repair Programme in Koror","Additionally, 4 schools (3 elementary and 1 high school in Koror) are repaired until they can be replaced with new buildings.",""]],"95":[[1,"74","11","Faculty Salary and Benefits Improvement","Improve salary and benefits packages for highly qualified faculty.",""],[1,"74","14","Teacher and School Principal Remuneration Improvement","Improve teacher and school principal remuneration and benefits.",""],[1,"75","8","Early Childhood Teacher Qualification Upgrade","Teachers with degrees in early childhood education will increase from 75% (2022) to 100% (2028).",""],[1,"75","8","Palau Community College Faculty and Scholarship Support","Improved faculty remuneration and benefits.",""],[1,"74","12","Student Incentive Packages for FSM and RMI Enrollment","Increase enrollment of students from the FSM and RMI by creating incentive packages (e.g., travel scholarships and financial aid packages) that target their specific needs.",""],[1,"75","8","Expanded Scholarship Packages for FSM and RMI Students","Improved scholarship packages offered to FSM and RMI students.",""],[1,"74","13","Online and Hybrid Higher Education Program Development Funding","Provide funding to support the development of online/hybrid bachelor's and master's degree programs so that critical partnerships with institutes of higher education in the U.S. can be further developed.",""],[1,"75","8","Hybrid Bachelor's and Master's Programme Development","New hybrid bachelor and master's programs introduced in partnership with U.S. Universities.",""],[1,"74","18","Remote and Online Learning Programs","Institutionalize remote/online learning programs.",""]],"96":[[1,"76","3","Electricity Infrastructure Maintenance and Development Programme","PPUC's investment program references the maintenance and development of the future of electricity, including the implementation of renewable electricity.",""],[1,"76","5","Renewable Energy Investment and Grid Upgrade Programme","Furthermore, there are calls for investment in the renewable energy sector, in recognition of Palau's potential as an energy exporter, including offshore wind power plants and the subsequent requirement of adoption of technologies that are new to the Palau electricity grid, as well as the upgrading, reinforcement, and construction of transmission lines.",""],[1,"76","5","Offshore Floating Solar Pilot Testing","Offshore PV solar plant installations floating on the ocean are currently being tested.",""],[1,"76","5","Offshore Energy Development Initiative","The development of offshore energy has the potential to deliver sustainable energy resources and the development of offshore wind is highlighted in PPUC's investment plan.",""],[1,"78","1","Independent Power Producer Electricity Procurement","PPUC could contract out a large fraction of the electricity generation to independent power producers (IPPs) through long-term power purchase contracts, at prices significantly lower than the cost of electricity generation through a diesel generating plant.",""],[1,"78","2","Floating Ocean PV Solar Pilot Projects","PV solar plant installations floating on the ocean are currently being tested as pilot projects in several countries.",""],[1,"78","2","Wind Power Generation by IPPs","wind turbines owned and operated by IPPs and installed on hilltops are also expected to provide a viable and cost-efficient green energy alternative to diesel generation.",""],[1,"78","4","Renewable Electricity Generation IPP Contracting","Electricity generation from renewables can be contracted out to IPPs, and therefore should not require any capital investment.",""],[1,"79","11","Private Investment Mobilization for Renewable Energy","and (ii) leveraging private investments to meet the country's renewable energy target.",""],[1,"80","1","Renewable Energy Transition through Long-Term Concessions and Power Purchase Agreements","The National Energy Master Plan, 2019 emphasizes efficiency and the transition from diesel generation to renewable energy through the introduction of long-term concessions and power purchase agreements (PPAs) to support private investments in renewable energy.",""],[1,"80","2","Renewable Energy Installation Programme","and (ii) increasing the supply of lower-cost energy through the installation of renewable energies.",""],[1,"82","1","Renewable Energy Transition and Grid Upgrade","For power generation, transmission, and distribution as well as renewable energy and energy efficiency, Palau has a goal of being 100% Renewable by 2035.",""],[1,"83","8","Renewable Energy Investment Expansion","Private investments in renewable energy with 45% of total energy supplied by renewables by FY25.",""]],"97":[[1,"77","1","Power Grid Reinforcement and Expansion","The transmission network will need to be extended to solar and wind power plants and reinforced to accept power from the proposed IPP- owned power plants.",""],[1,"78","7","Second 34.5 kV Transmission Circuit Between Aimeliik and Malakal","A second 34.5 kV circuit is required between these two generating stations.",""],[1,"79","1","Substation Rebuilding and Protection Upgrade","When the stations are rebuilt, additional protection and control devices should be included in their design.",""],[1,"79","2","Transmission Network Extension and Reinforcement","The transmission network will need to be extended to the selected location of solar and wind power plants and reinforced to accept power from the proposed IPP-owned power plants.",""],[1,"79","5","Electric Distribution Network Rehabilitation and Upgrade","Capital investments will be required over the next ten years to reconstruct the aged distribution lines, relocate lines to the shoulders of paved roads, and apply automated reclosers.",""],[1,"79","5","Small-Scale Generation Grid Connection Extensions","The 13.8 kV lines will also require some minor extensions to allow connection of small-scale generation, including a land-fill site generation facility.",""],[1,"80","5","Transmission Network Upgrade","Upgrade transmission network (Table 18).",""],[1,"83","19","Transmission Network Upgrade","III.2 Upgrade transmission network.",""],[1,"80","6","Ene-2 34.5 kV Line Construction","Ene-2 34.5 kV line construction to connect IPPs: Must be implemented, otherwise, Solar IPP cannot be operational even though the PV power plant is constructed.",""],[1,"80","7","34.5 kV Transmission Line Construction","o Ene-1 34.5 kV line construction to improve system stability:",""],[1,"81","6","34.5kV Line Construction to Connect IPPs","34.5kV line construction to connect IPPs",""],[1,"81","7","34.5kV Line Construction","34.5kV line construction to improve system stability",""],[1,"81","8","13.8kV Line Reconstruction","Reconstruction of 13.8kV lines",""],[1,"81","10","Rehabilitation of 34.5/13.8 kV Stations","Ene-3 Rehabilitation of 34.5/13.8 kV Stations: Rehabilitate all existing stations and provide 34.5 kV circuit breakers.",""],[1,"83","8","Electricity Transmission Network Upgrade","Upgraded transmission network by FY24.",""],[1,"83","8","Electricity Distribution Line Expansion","New distribution lines completed by FY26.",""],[1,"83","15","Establish Grid Code","II.2 Establish grid code.",""]],"98":[[1,"76","4","Backup Energy Source for Grid Stability","This will require a backup energy source to provide fast-speed frequency and voltage regulation, either in the form of battery storage and, or diesel generation.",""],[1,"77","1","Smart Meter Deployment for Loss Reduction","Automated revenue meters (Smart Meters) should be the most effective and cost-efficient solution for reducing energy pilferage and lowering operating costs.",""],[1,"78","3","Battery Storage and Backup Power for Renewable Grid Stability","For larger penetration of renewable energy sources, storage batteries would be required to maintain system stability.",""],[1,"80","8","Battery Energy Storage and Energy Management System Installation","Battery Energy Storage Systems and Energy Management System installed.",""],[1,"80","9","Grid Protection System Upgrade","Protection systems to reduce the frequent blackouts of the grid system will be installed.",""],[1,"83","27","Grid-Forming Battery Installation near Koror","Installation of a grid forming battery near Koror",""],[1,"81","12","Smart Meter Replacement Programme","Ene-6 Smart metering: Replace existing meters with smart meters.",""],[1,"83","8","Smart Meter Installation Programme","New smart meters installed by FY24.",""],[1,"81","3","Power System and Electric Mobility Capacity-Building Support","Capacity-building support provided.",""]],"99":[[1,"78","4","Diesel Backup Generator Replacement Investment","a part of the diesel generating plant, required as a backup energy source, will still require investment to replace generators as they reach the end of their service life.",""],[1,"79","11","Tariff Reform for PPUC Sustainability","Policy priorities are (i) tariff reforms to introduce market-driven incentives to enhance PPUC's sustainability",""],[1,"79","11","PPUC Financial Recovery Plan","The government has approved PPUC's financial recovery plan, which aims to restore liquidity and profitability.",""],[1,"80","2","Electricity Tariff Adjustment for PPUC Solvency","The energy sector will move to financial and economic self-sufficiency over the PDP period through (i) gradually increasing electricity tariffs to secure PPUC financial solvency,",""],[1,"80","3","Diesel Generating Plant Replacement and Generator Overhaul","The replacement of the diesel generating plant at the end of its service life with the larger generators requiring overhaul over the next 5 years.",""],[1,"80","4","Ene-5 Diesel Generating Station Replacement and Rehabilitation","Ene-5 Replacement and Rehabilitation of existing diesel generating stations:",""],[1,"83","8","Power Generation Plant Replacement","Replacement of the diesel-generating plant in FY24.",""],[1,"83","8","Electricity Tariff Adjustment for Viable Operations","Tariff increases provide for viable operations by FY25.",""],[1,"79","10","Human Resources Management Framework for PPUC","The overarching challenge is to unify the organization within a comprehensive human resources management framework and discontinue the use of public service practices.",""],[1,"79","10","PPUC Job Description and Performance Assessment Alignment","PPUC corporate plans need to be linked with job descriptions and performance assessments.",""],[1,"79","10","PPUC Office Accommodation Expansion","There is also a need to expand office accommodation, possibly on a new site.",""],[1,"81","13","New Office Accommodation for PPUC","New office accommodation at an estimated cost of $5,000,000, this amount includes possible land acquisition and construction.",""],[1,"81","14","Sustainable Investment Program","· Sustainable Investment Program (ADB's TA)105",""]],"100":[[1,"81","2","Electric Vehicle Charging Infrastructure Expansion","Enhance Electric Vehicle (EV) charging infrastructure.",""],[1,"81","13","Underground or Heavily Insulated Power Line Replacement Feasibility Study","In future fiscal years, PPUC will also consider the feasibility of replacing existing overhead lines with underground or heavily insulated transmission and distribution power lines, particularly in urban areas where it is difficult to maintain adequate clearances from structures.",""],[1,"83","14","Feasibility Study for Underground Power Lines in Urban Areas","Feasibility study of replacing existing overhead lines with underground in urban areas",""]],"101":[[1,"84","3","Mangrove Valuation and Sustainable Use Planning","Ongoing research to quantify the values of mangroves, including carbon storage values and sequestration site potential, and to determine rates of growth or decline is needed and assistance with planning for sustainable mangrove use is also needed.",""],[1,"84","4","Palau Forest Action Plan","A Palau Forest Action Plan108 is being implemented.",""],[1,"84","4","Forest Inventory and Analysis Monitoring Program","It is measured by the results of a 10- year repeated Forest Inventory and Analysis (FIA) program on 56 plots operated in cooperation with the US Forest Service that measures the extent, growth, composition, mortality, and health of forests as well as land use changes and potential for wildfire in the Republic.",""],[1,"84","4","Forest Land Use Planning Support","assistance with land use planning would ensure forests are incorporated into sustainable land management.",""],[1,"85","1","Sustainable Forest Management Policy Endorsement and Implementation","The Policy needs to be endorsed and implemented.",""],[1,"85","1","Forest Restoration and Invasive Species Actions","careful technical and land use planning, combined with restoration and invasive species actions, enable sustainable use or forest restoration while avoiding and minimizing threats from fire, invasive species, climate change, poor land use patterns, and other impacts are needed.",""],[1,"86","2","Forest and Landcover Restoration and Fire Prevention","Forest and landcover restoration and rehabilitation, combined with fire prevention and other threat abatements, is needed for highly erodible areas and needs to be done in partnership with communities.",""],[1,"88","1","National Nursery Operations Expansion","In the environment sector, continued and expanded operations of the national nursery are needed to maintain and increase forestry and food security efforts to rehabilitate land and reduce climate vulnerabilities across multiple sectors.",""],[1,"89","4","Forest Cover Maintenance and Expansion Support","State governments maintain and increase forest cover with national, technical, and financial support (Palau PAN and other funding mechanisms)",""],[1,"89","7","Forest, Mangrove, and Land Restoration and Erosion Control Programme","Forest, mangrove, and land research, planning, ecosystem restoration, landcover rehabilitation, and erosion control, and expanded nursery operations",""],[1,"90","9","Forest Policy and Action Plan Implementation","Forest Policy endorsed; Forest Action, Endangered Species, and IAS Species Response Plans in force",""]],"102":[[1,"85","2","Update Biodiversity and Endangered Species Regulations","many of the national laws and regulations protecting Palau's biodiversity are outdated and need to be updated",""],[1,"85","2","Develop and Enforce Endangered Species Regulations","Palau does not yet have national regulations for endangered species, although these are being advanced and when complete will need to be communicated and then enforced, along with the implementation of technical species recovery plans.",""],[1,"85","3","Invasive Alien Species Prevention, Control, and Eradication Measures","Invasive alien species pose a threat to Palau's native biodiversity, including agro- biodiversity, and require research and assessment, prevention, control, and eradication measures, consistent public and targeted outreach, and technical planning.",""],[1,"85","3","Cultural Programming Linking Nature and Culture","Many cultural practices are tightly linked to biodiversity, thus support for cultural programming that ties nature to culture is a priority.",""],[1,"85","3","Genetic Diversity Research and Access and Benefit Sharing Support","Understanding of genetic diversity is limited but necessary for Palau to implement its commitments to the convention on biological diversity, maintain agro-biodiversity, and benefit from Access and Benefit Sharing opportunities from the use of genetic data.",""],[1,"85","3","Expanded Invasive Species Protection Operations","Continued and expanded operations of invasive species protection, including preparation of species response plans and procedures are needed.",""],[1,"85","4","Protected Areas Network Financing Support","Protected areas in the PAN receive financial benefits from a portion of the Pristine Palau Environment Fee.",""],[1,"86","1","Protected Areas Strategy Implementation and Resourcing","Palau has a National PAN Strategy and Action Plan but needs resourcing to further implement it, particularly to improve compliance and enforcement in PAN sites and habitat restoration and climate adaptation.",""],[1,"86","1","Protected Areas Management Effectiveness Assessment Update","An update to a 2013-2014 Protected Areas Management Effectiveness (PAME) assessment is underway to measure the status of protected areas.",""],[1,"87","1","Invasive Alien Species Border Protection","The Division of Biosecurity in the Ministry of Finance has the responsibility of protecting Palau's borders from invasive alien species.","Ministry of Finance | Division of Biosecurity"],[1,"87","1","Species Protection Enforcement","The Division of Fish and Wildlife Protection (DFWP) in the Ministry of Justice enforces species protection.","Ministry of Justice | Division of Fish and Wildlife Protection (DFWP)"],[1,"88","2","Environmental Legal Framework Updates","Updates to several aspects of the environmental legal framework are needed in the next few years, including updates to the Biosecurity Act and regulations, marine protected area act and regulations, endangered species regulations, marine mammal act regulations; and the PAN Act's enforcement rules and regulations.",""],[1,"88","3","Protected Areas Expansion and PAN Rangers Compliance Role","The maintenance and growth of protected areas, including the expansion of roles of PAN Rangers to encourage compliance with multiple environmental and cultural laws, is a medium-term priority.",""],[1,"88","5","Invasive Alien Species Management and Prevention Program","Management of invasive alien species (IAS), including control of fruit flies, coconut rhinoceros beetles, and invasive vines, and prevention of new priority introductions such as brown tree snakes and tilapia, are important for food security.",""],[1,"88","5","Community-Based IAS Prevention and Control Institutionalization","Institutionalizing existing community-based IAS programs of prevention, awareness, reporting, and control (for which there is also proof of concept) is also an immediate priority for food-productive areas.",""],[1,"88","6","Rock Islands Southern Lagoon World Heritage Site Management and Enforcement","improving the management of the Rock Islands Southern Lagoon World Heritage Site (RISL) is a priority, with an emphasis on enforcement of the national and state legal framework.",""],[1,"89","9","Protected Areas Management Programme","Protected areas management (enforcement, education, restoration, climate adaptation)",""],[1,"89","11","Threat Abatement and Invasive Species Control Programme","Threat abatement, including invasive species prevention, control, and eradication where possible, development of species response plans, and fire prevention",""],[1,"89","14","Environmental and Species Law Monitoring and Enforcement","Monitoring, surveillance, and enforcement of environmental and species laws, regulations, and permit conditions, including expanded capacity to monitor via laboratory capacity",""],[1,"90","9","Invasive Species Management Programme","Improved invasive species management",""],[1,"90","9","Protected Area Site Management Improvement","Improved PAN site management",""],[1,"87","3","National Bird Monitoring and Heritage Conservation Programme","It is the home of the National Bird Monitoring Program and implements research and conservation activities on natural heritage and on links between biodiversity and culture.",""]],"103":[[1,"87","1","Environmental Governance Coordination and Enforcement","The Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries, and the Environment Bureau of Environment (BOE) coordinates and implements programs related to forests, biodiversity and protected or endangered species, freshwater quality, protected areas, threats such as invasive species, and community and public outreach on environmental stewardship.","Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries, and the Environment | Bureau of Environment (BOE)"],[1,"87","1","Environmental Regulation Implementation and Enforcement","The Palau Environmental Quality Protection Board (EQPB) is responsible for implementing, monitoring, and enforcing environmental regulations on (i) earthmoving, (ii) marine and freshwater quality, (iii) toilet and wastewater disposal facilities, (iv) solid waste management, (v) pesticides, (vi) public water supply systems, (vii) environmental impact statements, (viii) air pollution control, and (ix) ozone depleting substances.","Palau Environmental Quality Protection Board (EQPB)"],[1,"87","2","Cross-Ministry Environmental Coordination and Stewardship Support","MAFE's Office of Strategic Support Services (OSSS) coordinates cross-Ministry actions and leads communications to build awareness and environmental stewardship.","MAFE"],[1,"87","2","National Environmental Protection Council Secretariat","The Secretariat for the National Environmental Protection Council (NEPC), a cross-Ministry coordination body, sits in the Ministry of Finance.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"87","2","Environmental Donor Fund Channeling Mechanism","The NEPC Secretariat also serves as the focal point for many international granting mechanisms and is an important funnel for channeling international donor funds to environmental action on the ground.",""],[1,"87","2","SDG Measurement Coordination for Environment-Related Goals","The NEPC Secretariat also coordinates the measurement of SDGs, including SDGs 2,6, and 11-15, which are directly relevant to the Environment Sector.",""],[1,"87","2","Climate Change Policy and Action Plan Update","OCC is updating the Palau Climate Change Policy and Action Plan, which will identify climate adaptation, mitigation, and disaster response needs for 2024-2034.","Office of Climate Change"],[1,"87","2","Updated Climate Change Projections for Sector and Land Use Planning","OCC, NEMO, and the National Weather Office to update climate change projections that will then feed into the updated sector and land use plans.","Office of Climate Change | National Emergency Management Office | National Weather Office"],[1,"87","3","Environmental Regulations Enforcement Framework","Palau's eight sets of environmental regulations cover every aspect of the environment, with a primary benefit being the protection of water for human and habitat health and are implemented by EQPB.",""],[1,"87","3","PALARIS Spatial Analysis and Land-Use Planning Support","Spatial analyses conducted by PALARIS influence the selection of sites and land and marine use plans for every sector of Palau's development.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"88","3","Land Use Plan and Zoning Implementation","Implementation of land use plans and zoning, via mandated Planning Commissions and State Planning Offices, is an immediate priority, included in the Governance Pillar.",""],[1,"89","10","Community and Sector Land Use Planning Support","Community and sector land use planning, including spatial analyses and technical assistance",""],[1,"89","12","Environmental Laws and Regulations Update","· Update environmental laws and regulations",""],[1,"89","13","Environmental Communications and Awareness Programs","Environmental communications and awareness programs, including cultural programming and outreach on compliance with laws",""],[1,"90","9","Spatial Land Use Planning and Zoning Implementation","Spatial Land use planning and zoning implementation",""],[1,"90","9","Environmental Monitoring and Surveillance Expansion","Expanded environmental monitoring and smrveillance",""],[1,"90","9","Environmental Reporting and Outreach Strengthening","Updated and on-time international reports",""],[1,"90","9","Environmental Coordination and Mainstreaming Initiative","Improved coordination and mainstreaming",""]],"104":[[1,"92","4","Secured Transaction Registry","Recently enacted and upcoming legislation include: (i) Secured Transaction Registry - enacted and in place;",""],[1,"92","4","New Corporations Act Implementation","Recently enacted and upcoming legislation include: (ii) New Corporations Act - enacted and in the process of being implemented;",""],[1,"92","4","Private Bank and Trust Bank Legislation","Recently enacted and upcoming legislation include: (iii) Private Bank and Trust Bank Legislation - enacted, not implemented;",""],[1,"92","4","Digital Residency Act","Recently enacted and upcoming legislation include: (iv) Digital Residency Act - enacted and implemented;",""],[1,"92","4","Foreign Corporations Act Review","Recently enacted and upcoming legislation include: (v) Foreign Corporations Act - under review.",""],[1,"92","5","Digital Residency Program","The Digital Residency program is modeled after that of Estonia.",""],[1,"92","5","Stablecoin Pilot for Financial Inclusion","Palau is implementing a Stablecoin pilot to improve financial inclusion and access.",""],[1,"92","8","SME Finance and Market Access Improvements","Market improvements - Enhanced financial literacy, improved access to finance for Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs), improved environment for business, improved consumer access to financial services in rural and outlying areas, increased Fintech options, and improved access to stakeholders abroad, and",""],[1,"92","9","Financial Sector Macro System Improvements","Macro System Improvements - Development of components for the financial sector, expansion of oversight to all financial institutions, and upgrade capacity with government and regulators.",""],[1,"93","5","Financial Sector Legislation Reform","Legislation is passed that creates a safer and more equitable financial environment.",""],[1,"93","8","Financial Literacy Program","MOE establishes and implements financial literacy program by FY25.","MOE"],[1,"93","8","Financial Sector Access and Inclusion Measures","Improve access to finance and financial services (ongoing).",""],[1,"93","8","Financial Sector Legal Protection Reform","Legislation passed for the protection of land, bankruptcy, and consumer credit protection by end of FY25.",""],[1,"93","13","Private Business Environment Improvement Initiatives","Political support for initiatives to improve the environment for private business.",""],[1,"93","13","Financial Literacy Programs","MOE and private sector implement improved financial literacy programs.","MOE"],[1,"93","19","Financial Literacy Programs","Develop and implement financial literacy programs for schools, individuals, and SMEs.",""],[1,"93","17","New Technology for Improved Financial Access","Increase the use of new technology for improved financial access.",""],[1,"93","22","Technology Solutions Research and Implementation","Research and implement technology solutions with assistance of ADB, IMF and WB",""],[1,"93","23","Fintech Regulatory and Technical Support","Provide regulatory and technical support for the implementation of Fintech solutions",""],[1,"93","24","Credit Bureau Development and Operation","Develop and operate a Credit Bureau",""],[1,"93","25","Online Land Registry Implementation","Research and implement an online land registry with assistance of ADB, IMF and WB",""],[1,"93","26","Legislation for Land, Bankruptcy, and Consumer Credit Protection","Introduce Legislation for Protection of Land, Bankruptcy, and Consumer Credit Protection",""]],"105":[[1,"92","6","Social Security and Civil Service Pension Reform","Working groups were formed to consider reforms that would ensure the long-term financial sustainability of SS and CSPP.",""],[1,"93","13","Social Security and Civil Service Pension Plan Stabilization","Political support to prevent the collapse of Social Security and Civil Service Pension Plan.",""]],"106":[[1,"95","5","Sustainable Fisheries Catch Adjustment and Pelagic Fishery Expansion","Increasing pelagic fishery production and consumption to shift pressure away from coastal fisheries, and aligning nearshore fishery production with sustainable limits that consider the impacts of climate change are immediate priorities.",""],[1,"96","1","Fishery Data Collection and Stock Assessment System","The development and deployment of consistent data collection protocols and the establishment of Stock Assessments and Harvest Assessments are needed to track fishery production and consumption and to enable adaptive management to be climate resilient.",""],[1,"96","5","Marine Spatial Planning and Marine Protected Area Review","Marine Spatial Planning (MSP) was underway in 2023.",""],[1,"97","4","Strengthened International Engagement on Fisheries and Marine Spatial Planning","Continued engagement with international partners and with the PNA is an immediate priority, including Palau taking a more active leadership role in scaling up marine spatial planning to the Micronesian region.",""],[1,"99","4","Marine Spatial Planning Coordination and Data Sharing System","The MSP exercise for all of Palau's marine waters from shore to the edge of the Exclusive Economic Zone requires sustained and supported coordination among all fishery and aquaculture sector partners.",""],[1,"99","4","Marine Data Management and Adaptive Feedback Systems","Monitoring and Data and information sharing among and between these agencies is a critical need, but there are few established data management systems to improve data sharing and feedback systems, and adaptive management.",""],[1,"99","4","Climate Fisheries Research Capacity Expansion","expanding research capacity to develop and track climate shifts and impacts is needed.",""],[1,"100","1","National and State Fishery Policy Alignment and Regulatory Update","investment in new and aligned National and State Fishery Policies is warranted and an immediate need.",""],[1,"100","1","Marine Protection Act Update and Fisheries Registration System","An update to the Marine Protection Act and its regulations is underway and should include a registration and permitting system to better generate and track data.",""],[1,"100","1","Fisheries Education, Outreach, and Compliance Support","Education and outreach are needed to facilitate the uptake of best practices and to encourage compliance with updated laws.",""],[1,"100","2","Nearshore Fisheries Resilience Planning and Regulatory Reform","Priorities include (i) comprehensive planning for commercial and subsistence fishing; (ii) updates to a regulatory regime to usher in changes to seasons and size restrictions, (iii) marine protected areas, and more; an increase in public outreach and engagement with fishers; and (iv) improvement and sophistication of enforcement to encourage compliance with the updated regime.",""],[1,"100","13","Fisheries Policy and Regulatory Framework Review and Update","Undertake a comprehensive review and update and implement fisheries and fisheries- related policy and regulatory framework.",""],[1,"101","1","Fisheries and Aquaculture Data Collection and Monitoring System","Develop and implement data collection protocols for coastal/nearshore and pelagic fisheries, and for aquaculture, implement monitoring, and create data sharing mechanisms and adaptive management feedback loops, with capacity building",""],[1,"101","2","Fisheries Research and Assessment Programme","Implement research to develop stock and harvest assessments, market studies and goods-and-services value evaluations, sustainable use parameters, and climate projections and adaptation needs for nearshore, offshore, and invertebrate fisheries, including a better understanding of the fisheries markets, their scale, and their main barriers and drivers",""],[1,"101","3","Fisheries Law and Policy Update","Update relevant fishery laws, policies, and best practices, including spatial plans",""],[1,"101","6","Expanded Participation in Fisheries Dialogues","Expand engagement and participation in bilateral, regional, and international fisheries dialogues, with regional scaling",""]],"107":[[1,"96","4","Fisheries Market Research and Value Chain Support","Investment into research and support services to facilitate improved fisheries marketing and aligning supply and value chains is needed.",""],[1,"96","6","Support for Anchored Fish Attracting Device Fisheries Network","the future of this fishery is dependent on reliable access to a productive aFAD network that is supported by stable and continued funding by the Palau Bureau of Fisheries (BOF).",""],[1,"97","1","Launch NRFC Initiatives with Donated Co-operatively Owned Vessels","in Palau could benefit from financial and technical support to launch similar NRFC initiatives with co-operatively owned vessels donated by Palau's international partners.",""],[1,"97","1","Multi-Agency Coordination for NRFC Initiatives","These types of initiatives require careful coordination between agencies, state governments, and the private sector.",""],[1,"97","2","Acquire and Test Bouke-Ami Baiting Net for BOFI","this style of net should be acquired for BOFI and tested to increase the baiting performance of the fishery.",""],[1,"97","2","Long-Term Institutional Capacity Building for the Fisheries Sector","long-term institutional capacity building that anticipates the needs of the sector is needed.",""],[1,"97","3","Domestic Pelagic Fishing Industry Development","The PNMS Act includes provisions for a new domestic pelagic fishing industry to support the local market.",""],[1,"97","3","Strategic Partnerships for Local Fishing Fleet Development","Palau is exploring strategic partnerships to develop a local fishing fleet, establish a central fish auction market, build processing, and wharf facilities, and identify value-added products that can be developed from excess catch or by-catch.",""],[1,"97","3","Fish Supply Chain Infrastructure Investment","Investment in this infrastructure throughout the supply chain is needed, as is sustained engagement with international partners.",""],[1,"99","1","Digital Marketplace for Fishery Producers and Buyers","investment into innovative business models or a digital marketplace to connect producers with buyers is needed.",""],[1,"99","1","Fishery Market Assessment and Analysis","Data to improve financial benefits, including market assessments and analyses, are also needed to improve marketing, pricing, and livelihood benefits.",""],[1,"99","1","Hook to Fork High-Value Fishery Model","A digital marketplace could also help retain the high value of fishery products and enable a \"Hook to Fork\" high-value model.",""],[1,"100","3","Cooperative Association Capacity-Building Support","Investment into cooperative associations, like the NRFC, particularly to build their business and entrepreneurial skills is needed.",""],[1,"100","3","Local Ranger Training and Legal Alignment","Training and alignment of laws are also needed for local Rangers.",""],[1,"101","4","Interagency and Public-Private Coordination Mechanism","Strengthen coordination mechanisms that allow for meaningful collaboration between agencies, state governments, and the private sector",""],[1,"101","8","Community Enforcement Capacity Building","Capacity building to improve enforcement capacity in communities",""],[1,"101","7","Domestic Tuna Fisheries and Aquaculture Market Development","Explore innovative business models or digital marketplaces that may involve both government and the private sector to develop domestic tuna fisheries and aquaculture",""],[1,"101","9","Aquaculture and Fisheries Supply Chain Infrastructure Investment","Invest in critical infrastructure in the aquaculture and fisheries supply chains, including research capacity to track impacts of climate change, and improve access to loans for private businesses",""],[1,"102","3","Fishery and Aquaculture Production Expansion","To help diversify the economy and improve food security by increasing fishery and aquaculture production and food system employment opportunities.",""],[1,"102","7","Support for Fisheries Catch Distribution, Marketing, and Local Purchase","Distribution and marketing of fisheries catch, and purchase of local catch is supported by a growing private sector.",""]],"108":[[1,"103","5","Free Preventive Health Services and Subsidized Health Care","The Palau Constitution mandates the government, through the MHHS to provide free preventive health services and subsidized health care for citizens.","MHHS"],[1,"103","6","Palau Healthcare Fund and National Health Insurance Scheme","To implement the health mandate sustainably, the Palau Healthcare Fund (HCF) was established in 2010 and consists of two components, individual medical savings accounts (MSA) and a pooled universal social health insurance fund commonly known as National Health Insurance (NHI).",""],[1,"104","1","National Health Insurance Coverage for Catastrophic Illnesses and Medical Referrals","NHI complements MSA by providing coverage for catastrophic illnesses and off-island referrals approved as medically necessary by a Medical Referral Committee established within the MHHS.",""],[1,"104","1","Government-Paid Medical Savings Account Premium Support","The government pays the MSA premiums for unemployed senior citizens and the severely disabled using funds earmarked for this purpose from tobacco taxes.",""],[1,"104","2","Health Financing and Revenue Collection Reform","This shortfall prevents MHHS from hiring more qualified healthcare workers, improving service delivery to all states and rural areas, upscaling information technology and databases, and funding capital investments such as a new hospital facility and, or clinics and housing for expatriate health workers.","MHHS"],[1,"107","13","Continued Prioritization of Health under the New Compact","Administration & OEK will continue to prioritize health.",""]],"109":[[1,"104","3","College of Health Program Revitalization","MHHS is planning to revitalize the College of Health128 program to ensure patient care is not affected while the existing workforce is upskilled, and new health workers are trained.",""],[1,"104","4","Health Service Performance Assessment and Quality Improvement","Assessing service performance can be done by conducting patient satisfaction surveys, doing walkthroughs of problem areas, and collecting feedback from the staff.",""],[1,"104","4","Revision of Health Policies and Standard Operating Procedures","This helps identify quality assurance and improvement gaps that can be addressed by revision of policies and Standard Operating Practices (SOPs), using newer and more efficient methods, and adjusting patient flow by changing the setup of the clinics or other service areas.",""],[1,"104","7","College of Health Educational Enhancement Initiative","College of Health is an initiative that began in 2011 as the Ministry of Health's internal entity devoted to the educational enhancement of its staff, the community, and potential future employees.","Ministry of Health"],[1,"105","7","Electronic Health Record and Medication Supply Tracking System","Project Olangch was launched in November 2022 that includes Tamanu which is the electronic health record system being used in the hospital along with M-Supply that will track medication levels to ensure a continuous supply",""],[1,"105","14","Health System Strengthening Support","JICA support to Bureau of Hospital Service for health system strengthening",""],[1,"105","18","Health Systems Strengthening and Service Delivery Improvement","The government is attempting to improve the appropriateness, staffing, management, monitoring, and overall delivery of all health services",""],[1,"105","18","Community Health Responsibility Promotion","and to encourage the community to take responsibility for their own health.",""],[1,"106","1","Health System Strengthening","Recently, MHHS has focused on two major short-term objectives (2022-2024) that will help bridge gaps in services and build on efficiencies.",""],[1,"106","1","Health Improvement Framework","Recently, MHHS has focused on two major short-term objectives (2022-2024) that will help bridge gaps in services and build on efficiencies.",""],[1,"106","2","Health Workforce Development","Objective 1 focuses on strengthening 5 strategic areas namely (i) health workforce development,",""],[1,"106","2","Health Information Standards Development","Objective 1 focuses on strengthening 5 strategic areas namely (ii) health information standards and development,",""],[1,"106","2","Health Sector Strategic Planning, Communications, and Reporting","Objective 1 focuses on strengthening 5 strategic areas namely (iii) strategic planning, communications, and reporting,",""],[1,"106","2","Health Standards, Quality Assurance, and Quality Improvement","Objective 1 focuses on strengthening 5 strategic areas namely (v) standards, quality assurance and quality improvement.",""],[1,"107","8","Patient-Centered Primary Care Realignment","A patient-centered approach is applied where all services are available at each visit to save time and be more effective in capturing diseases early.",""],[1,"107","8","Primary Care Realignment for Population Health","Realign primary care to support population health.",""],[1,"107","8","Client-Patient Satisfaction Survey System","Client-patient satisfaction surveys are available at 100% of service delivery points and baseline assessment is conducted by QA/QI coordinator.",""],[1,"107","8","College of Health Professional Development and Licensure Oversight","College of Health is developed to oversee professional development initiatives and licensure requirements and ensure minimum core competency standards are completed for 100% of healthcare workers.",""],[1,"107","8","Workforce Wellness Program","Workforce Wellness Program initiated with dedicated staff to ensure program continuity.",""],[1,"107","8","Ministry-Wide Health Information System","Ministry-wide Health Information System is 100%.",""],[1,"107","8","Integrated Care System for IPV and MCH Populations","An integrated system of care will be instituted to support IPV and MCH populations.",""]],"110":[[1,"104","5","Health Facility Capital Repair and Rehabilitation","Some of the existing buildings require major capital repairs and rehabilitation to reliably provide health services.",""],[1,"104","5","Health Facility Space Expansion and Service Reorganization","The existing buildings do not provide sufficient space for all health sector services and some services must be scheduled to share existing infrastructure.",""],[1,"104","5","Health Facility Maintenance and Staff Training Partnership","MHHS carries out building maintenance assisted by the Transportation and Equipment Department and from time to time, the Bureau of Public Works, and local and outside contractors.",""],[1,"104","5","Maintenance Personnel Skills Training with Palau Community College","MHHS partners with Palau Community College to provide training for maintenance personnel to enhance their skills.",""],[1,"105","3","Development of Mini Hospitals in Melekeok and Peleliu","The Ministry plans to further develop the main community health centers in Melekeok and Peleliu into mini hospitals.","Ministry"],[1,"105","4","New Public Health and Administration Building","MOH has a 10-year plan to build a new public health and administration building.","MOH"],[1,"105","5","Medical Equipment Replacement and BNH Facility Improvement","Old medical equipment needs to be replaced and improvements made at the current BNH while work is underway for a new hospital.",""],[1,"105","8","Telehealth Systems Development","Telehealth systems are being developed in partnership with Taiwan, Japan, New Zealand, and Australia for training, diagnosis, and treatment planning",""],[1,"105","9","Telehealth and Telemedicine Specialist Consultation System","A new telehealth/telemedicine equipment and system for specialist consultation with Shin Kong Hospital is being developed through a partnership with Taiwan",""],[1,"105","10","MRI Installation and Staff Training","An MRI donated by Japan has been received and positioned inside Radiology Department pending staff training for operations",""],[1,"105","11","Intensive Care Unit Expansion Donation","Japan has donated a 4-bed Intensive Care Unit to expand the medical ward ICU; operation of the unit is pending additional staff to be able to use it",""],[1,"105","12","Portable X-Ray Machine Installation","Installation of a portable x-ray machine at Central Community Health Center in Koror",""],[1,"105","13","Emergency Radio Communication System Enhancement","Enhancement of Emergency Radio Communication System with the Southwest Islands to assist with the response to health emergencies completed in December 2022",""],[1,"105","15","Transition Unit for Elderly Patients Requiring 24-Hour Care","Transition Unit opening in summer 2023 for elderly patients who require 24-hour care",""],[1,"105","16","Hemodialysis Capacity Expansion","Additional 6 hemodialysis units under formal bid process to augment existing 12 units",""],[1,"106","2","BNH Relocation, MHHS Administration, and Public Health Building","Objective 1 focuses on strengthening 5 strategic areas namely (iv) BNH relocation, MHHS administration, and public health building,",""],[1,"106","4","Health Facility Equipment Replacement and Upgrading","Replacement of other medical equipment including a new incinerator, an energy-efficient lighting system, new plumbing systems, a radio center, major medical equipment, and major general equipment",""],[1,"106","6","New Hospital Construction","Priority Capital Programs are a new hospital at an estimated cost of $120 million",""],[1,"106","6","Public Health Facility Construction","and a new Public Health facility at an estimated cost of $25 million.",""],[1,"107","20","Health Facility Equipment and Infrastructure Upgrades","Water cooling system at $500,000, Water sprinkler system at $800,000, Water filtration system at $350,000, Hyperbaric chamber $200,000, Oxygen generation plant $500,000, Medical waste incinerator $40,000, Laundry equipment $25,000, Kitchen equipment $25,000, Laboratory to allow for CLIA certification $100,000, and Cardiac catheterization laboratory $500,000.",""]],"111":[[1,"108","4","National Housing Commission for Housing Development Loan Project Administration","the National Housing Commission (NHC) was created to administer the Housing Development Loan Project (HDLP) and address issues relating to the development of residential housing in Palau.",""],[1,"108","4","National Housing Coordination and Policy Development","This includes coordinating services between the National Development Bank of Palau, Palau Housing Authority (PHA), the States, relevant agencies, and citizens, along with adopting a National Housing Policy.",""],[1,"108","6","Affordable Housing Supply Expansion","Find a solution to housing problems by making homes available at an affordable price and increasing the supply of housing.",""],[1,"108","7","Green Communities and Housing Subdivision Development","Coordinate the development of green communities, revival of old villages, and establishment of new housing subdivisions.",""],[1,"108","8","Affordable Multi-Family Housing Construction Support","Support the construction of affordable multi-family dwellings to provide housing for short-term periods.",""],[1,"108","9","Affordable Housing Access Support","Provide access to affordable housing for citizens in need, prioritizing displaced citizens and first-time homeowners.",""],[1,"108","10","Public Land Housing Subdivision Investment","This will require investment in housing subdivisions on public lands.",""],[1,"109","3","Social Housing Support Loan Programme","Social housing support to those earning less than US$35,300 per annum is being provided by the Palau Housing Authority (PHA).",""],[1,"109","3","New Housing Construction and Renovation Loans","The programs, arranged through low-interest 30-year loans, include (i) new housing construction, (ii) housing renovation and, or extension, (iii) home repair and improvement (from fire or water damage), (iv) emergency housing reconstruction, and (v) water harvesting and storage.",""],[1,"109","3","National Development Bank Housing Loan Access","For those above this earnings threshold, access to loans is available through the National Development Bank of Palau (NDBP).",""],[1,"109","9","Affordable Housing Infrastructure Support","The development of affordable housing on Babeldaob and the outlying communities requires planned housing development and must be supported by adequate and accessible basic infrastructure such as roads, water and sanitation, solid waste management, electricity, telecommunications, and transportation.",""],[1,"109","10","Culturally Integrated Housing Development","Any housing development needs to be cognizant of Palauan culture and should include, within the housing development plan, cultural facilities and, or restoration or upgrades to existing cultural sites.",""],[1,"110","2","State Housing Subdivision Development on Public Land","Every State has identified and or begun construction of housing subdivisions on public land to create more housing stock and attract more residents to come home.",""],[1,"110","2","Public-Private Housing Partnership Initiative","There have also been some private-public partnerships to create more housing.",""],[1,"112","8","Babeldaob Housing and Neighborhood Infrastructure Development","Infrastructure to support housing and neighborhood development is constructed each year in Babeldaob.",""],[1,"112","8","Pilot Housing Subdivision Construction in Babeldaob","Pilot housing subdivision is constructed in Babeldaob in 2026 in whichever state ready to proceed.",""],[1,"112","24","Regional Infrastructure for Housing and Neighborhood Development","Develop regional infrastructure to support housing and neighborhood development in Babeldaob",""]],"112":[[1,"110","3","Coastal Community Protection and Relocation","As sea levels rise impacted communities in coastal areas will need to be protected, this may include relocation to higher ground.",""],[1,"110","6","Housing Policy Planning Process","A policy planning process is needed to raise awareness of housing issues and to identify coordinated strategies, policies, and actions to ensure that the housing needs of Palau's population are met.",""],[1,"111","1","Comprehensive Housing Assessment and Housing Policy","A comprehensive housing assessment is required, accompanied by a housing policy that identifies existing housing inventory, land suitable for housing including subdivisions, homes likely to be affected by climate change, and new building technologies thus ensuring Palauan access to safe and affordable homes.",""],[1,"111","1","Assessment of Multi-dwelling and Condominium Housing Options","This comprehensive assessment shall also explore and assess the applicability of multi-dwelling residences, condominiums, and other accommodations to alleviate the increasing gap between the demand for affordable housing and available supply.",""],[1,"112","8","Comprehensive Housing Policy Development and Approval","The comprehensive housing policy is completed and approved by the end of 2025.",""],[1,"112","8","Revision of PNCA 34","PNCA 34 is reviewed and revised by the end of 2024.",""],[1,"112","8","State-Level Comprehensive Land Use Planning","Comprehensive land use plans are completed for all States by the end of 2025.",""],[1,"112","8","Climate-Impacted Housing Compensation and Subdivision Planning","Identify areas and homes that are likely to be impacted by climate change are identified, compensation legislation and policy developed, and lands suitable for housing subdivisions for impacted individuals identified by the end of 2025.",""],[1,"112","8","Housing Materials and Construction Methods Innovation Strategy","New construction materials and methodologies investigated, and an education strategy developed and implemented by the end of 2026.",""],[1,"112","15","Comprehensive Housing Needs Assessment","Conduct a comprehensive housing needs assessment",""],[1,"112","16","Comprehensive Housing Policy","II.2 Establish an effective and comprehensive housing policy",""],[1,"112","18","Comprehensive Land Use Planning for All States","Complete comprehensive land use plans for all States (GEF 6)",""],[1,"112","19","Policy to Protect Homes in Climate-Vulnerable Communities","Develop policy to protect homes in communities likely to be impacted by climate change",""],[1,"112","20","Construction Materials and Methodologies Innovation Programme","Investigate and introduce new construction materials and methodologies, develop and implement education",""],[1,"112","21","Subdivision Planning Standards and Building Code Adoption","Prepare and adopt subdivision planning standards and building code",""],[1,"112","22","Construction Sector Professionalization Legislation","Increase levels of professionalism in the construction sector by developing and enacting legislation",""]],"113":[[1,"113","3","Second Submarine Cable Connectivity Project","Accordingly, new ICT businesses will likely only begin to consider Palau once PC2 is in place.",""],[1,"114","4","Belau Submarine Cable Corporation Core Network Development","Development of the Belau Submarine Cable Corporation, (BSCC) core network to eliminate single points of failure and deliver cost-effective high-speed connectivity",""],[1,"114","6","Universal High-Speed Connectivity Expansion","· Capable Customer Access - Universal, cost-effective, high-speed connectivity (high speed in this context means 25 / 5 Mbps and beyond symmetrical mobile and fixed connections - i.e., same speeds for upload and download).",""],[1,"114","6","Long-Term 100/25 Mbps Network Upgrade","The longer-term objective is to build a network capable of 100 / 25 Mbps customer access where practicable.",""],[1,"114","7","LTE Mobile Coverage Expansion","Required expansion of infrastructure to be partially funded by USO via a tender process.",""],[1,"114","7","Multiple Mobile Networks Resilience Approach","The ICT sector recommends Palau should be served through multiple physical mobile networks for resilience.",""],[1,"114","14","Mobile Network Upgrade","Upgrade existing mobile network",""],[1,"114","15","Mobile Network Upgrade and Expansion","Upgrade and expand mobile network",""],[1,"115","5","Nationwide FTTP and Mobile Broadband Expansion","Expansion and improvement of ICT services by the two telecommunications SOE's (PNCC & BSCC), the Government and the private sector.",""],[1,"115","8","Off-Island Capacity Expansion and Redundancy Upgrade","Provide extended access to off-island capacity to all operators via the Babeldaob Loop - to be in service by the end of 2023.",""],[1,"115","8","Mobile Network Upgrade and Coverage Expansion","PNCC will upgrade its current 4G network in these areas by end 2023.",""],[1,"115","8","National Broadband and Fiber-to-the-Premises Rollout","Fast, reliable fixed-line broadband services to every home, business, and Govt. building throughout RoP by the end 2026.",""],[1,"115","10","BSCC Network Connection and Nationwide Coverage Expansion","BSCC can connect to the main trunk through partner Trans-Pacific Networks (TPN) by Q2 2024.",""],[1,"115","20","PNCC Mobile Network Replacement and Expansion","PNCC Mobile Network Replacement / Expansion c)",""]],"114":[[1,"113","5","Universal Service Funding Review","This may require re-addressing the funding of universal service.",""],[1,"113","5","Telecommunications Infrastructure Sharing Framework Review","The theme of the 2017 Telecommunications Act - sharing of core infrastructure with competition at retail - remains valid but will need to be revisited to accommodate new factors 133 that have emerged in the last five years.",""],[1,"113","5","Targeted Rural Connectivity Regulation","It is important that limited regulatory resources are directed toward areas of greatest need.",""],[1,"113","6","Telecommunications Competition and Universal Service Reform","Regulation that encourages fair competition on a commercial basis for the improvement of telecommunications services for all of Palau and encourages expansion via a revitalized Universal Service Obligation (USO) process.",""],[1,"113","6","Universal Service Area Definition Study","This would require a study to define the USO areas.",""],[1,"113","6","Universal Service Customer Subsidies","Here the solution may be subsidies for certain USO customers.",""],[1,"113","7","Critical National Infrastructure Protection Framework","Protection of critical national infrastructure, by identifying critical assets, and implementing appropriate processes, regulations, and legislation.",""],[1,"114","1","Telecommunications Regulatory and Legislative Reform","Re-framing of regulations and legislation to accommodate the dynamic changes in the sector e.g., where attention is monetized by \"over the top\", often global, providers who make no contribution to the costs of local networks or to local tax revenues.",""],[1,"114","2","Telecommunications Infrastructure Investment Incentive Reform","Creating a legal and regulatory environment that encourages investment in critical telecommunications infrastructure.",""],[1,"114","3","Tax Removal on Consumer Telecommunications Equipment","Supporting equitable conditions for the adoption of technology and innovation in Palau for all citizens regardless of their socio-economic status, through the removal of all taxation on the import and sale of consumer telecommunications equipment.",""],[1,"115","7","Universal Service Obligation Enforcement and Nationwide Coverage Expansion","The law on USO is enforced and nationwide coverage is delivered through a sustainable 'Play or Pay' approach to ensure access for all Palauans.",""]],"115":[[1,"115","8","Government Services Portal Expansion","Increase ease of access to Government services via Government Services Portal.",""],[1,"115","8","Tax Online System Implementation","Increase the efficiency of tax collection process via Tax Online system.",""],[1,"115","8","National Cybersecurity Policy","Protect the data of citizens and businesses via National Cybersecurity Policy.",""],[1,"115","8","Cybercrimes Act","Provide regulation and framework for punishment of illegal activity online in Palau via Cybercrimes Act.",""],[1,"115","8","National Financial Management System Rollout","Full rollout of the National Financial Management System.",""],[1,"115","8","Customs Single Window Project","Increase efficiency, volume and value of customers collection via Customs Single Window Project (ASYCUDA)",""]],"116":[[1,"114","10","Industry-Level Disaster Preparedness Support","Preparedness - Industry-level support for Disaster Preparedness coordinated via NEMO.",""],[1,"114","10","Cell Broadcast Emergency Alert System","Cell Broadcast for all mobile operators by 2025 to enable rapid dissemination of critical safety information.",""]],"117":[[1,"116","4","Law Enforcement Infrastructure and Training Complex Development","The MOJ is developing standard rules and operating procedures while building a centralized law enforcement complex.","MOJ"],[1,"116","4","Regional Maritime Training Center Establishment","The MOJ also plans to establish a regional maritime training center within the existing compound of Marine Law in Malakal.","MOJ"],[1,"117","3","Marine Monitoring Station Construction","Grant aid from Japan for up to 500 million yen (approximately $4.8 million) recently provided the government with a set of equipment to build two monitoring stations in Ngeremlengui and Malakal.",""],[1,"117","12","K9 Narcotics Detection Program Funding","The current K9 Program needs funding to enable stronger detection of narcotics at our air and seaports as well as postal services.",""],[1,"117","14","Police Capacity and Justice Delivery Improvement","The government intends to improve the police coverage, staffing, management, technology integration, and overall efficiency and effectiveness of carrying out justice in the Republic from proactive intervention and community policing to investigations, case management,",""],[1,"119","8","Port Inspection and K9 Handler Capacity Expansion","Increase inspections and surveillance of our ports through cross-utilization of our K9 program and to increase the number of officers trained as K9 Handlers.",""],[1,"119","8","Police Data Transparency and Public Statistics System","Capture intake (reports), investigations, and prosecution data and create and make statistics public to maintain transparency and public accountability.",""],[1,"119","8","MOJ Facilities Repair and Replacement Programme","MOJ offices and facilities are either repaired or replaced to provide an optimum work environment by 2025.",""],[1,"118","7","Parole Officers Program","Establish a parole officers' program to ensure the rehabilitation of inmates and to reduce recidivism.",""],[1,"118","8","K9 Program Strengthening","Strengthening of the K9 Program",""],[1,"118","10","CCTV Coverage Expansion in Key Areas","CCTV coverage for key areas that do not have CCTVs, especially in Koror and Airai",""],[1,"119","8","Corrections Rehabilitation Programme","Having a suitable Division of Corrections in place with proper rehab programs in place.",""]],"118":[[1,"117","2","New Relocated Correctional Facility in Ngchesar","Short-term infrastructure improvements including fencing and the addition of CCTV equipment were made to the Koror Jail and as part of the government's strategy, a plan for a new and relocated correctional facility began to be implemented.",""],[1,"117","10","Completion of the New Prison","The new prison needs to be completed but there is a lack of additional funding due to piecemeal appropriations.",""],[1,"118","6","Completion of New Prison Capital Project","Additional capital to complete the new prison.",""],[1,"119","22","New Prison Construction and Furnishing in Ngchesar","Complete construction of and furnish new Prison in Ngchesar",""]],"119":[[1,"118","3","Expansion of Substations and Emergency Response Capacity","Expanding substations to include both police units and fire and ambulatory services to ensure consistent response times in all parts of Babeldaob, including the provision of vehicles and equipment.",""],[1,"118","4","Fire Tanker Replacement and Expansion","Additional fire tankers in Koror and Babeldaob to replace old fire engines.",""],[1,"118","5","Fire Hydrant System Upgrade","The fire hydrant system needs to be updated to ensure faster refill and response time.",""]],"120":[[1,"121","6","Waste Segregation and Recycling Improvement","Improving waste management through segregation and recycling (to reduce inputs to dumps) is an immediate priority,",""],[1,"121","6","Marine Debris Flow Management","Managing the flow of marine debris is a medium- to long-term priority for communities.",""],[1,"122","1","Waste Tires Shredding Project","Waste tires shredding project.",""],[1,"122","2","Scrap Metal Collection and Recycling Contract","BPW has a contract (Contract No. 12-029) with Palau Waste Collection to collect all scrap metal entering the M-dock landfill for recycling purposes.","BPW | Palau Waste Collection"],[1,"122","2","Redeemed Beverage Container Recovery and Shipping","The contract also includes buying and shipping out redeemed beverage containers (steel, aluminum, and plastics) from the recycling program (RPPL 7-24).",""],[1,"122","3","Recycling Program","· Recycling Program (RPPL 7-24).",""],[1,"122","4","Waste Management Awareness Programs","Awareness programs are conducted throughout the year to promote the 3Rs, waste segregation, and the importance of best waste management practices.",""],[1,"122","6","Zero Waste Society Promotion Project","International Center Environmental Technology Transfer (ICETT) \"project of working together with the government and the citizens for zero waste society promotion in the Republic of Palau\".",""],[1,"122","7","Regional Solid Waste Management Technical Cooperation Project","Japanese Technical Cooperation Project for Promotion of Regional Initiatives on Solid Waste Management in Pacific Island Countries Phase II (JPRISM II).",""],[1,"122","8","National Solid Waste Management Strategy and Action Plan","A new National Solid Waste Management Strategy (NSWMS) and its action plan were prepared in line with the Cleaner Pacific (2016-2025) and officially submitted to the Minister.",""],[1,"122","13","Scrap Metal and Beverage Container Recycling Contract","Service Contract No. 12-029 with Palau Waste Collection to collect all scrap metal entering the M-dock landfill for recycling purposes.",""],[1,"122","14","Recycling Program Redemption Center Operations Contract","Service Contract No. 16-084 with Belau Garbage and Scrap Company for the company to operate as a redemption center under the recycling program (RPPL 7-24).",""],[1,"122","15","Beverage Container Recycling Redemption Center Arrangement","MOU with KSG to operate as an initial redemption center under the Beverage Container Recycling Regulations (RPPL 7-24).",""],[1,"124","6","Scrap Metal Storage Area Establishment","Scrap metal storage area established by FY25.",""],[1,"124","6","Private Recycler Incentive Scheme","Private company recyclers incentives established by FY26.",""],[1,"124","6","Recycling Programme Expansion","Recycling program expanded by FY24.",""],[1,"124","6","Advance Recovery Fee and Deposit Scheme","Advance Recovery Fee & Deposit (ARFD) established by FY25.",""],[1,"124","19","Advance Recovery Fee and Deposit Scheme","Establish Advance Recovery Fee & Deposit (ARFD) towards sound material cycle society is developed and a legal framework for at least one problematic waste stream is developed.",""],[1,"124","14","Designated Scrap Metal Recycling Area Near National Landfill","Identify a designated area near the National landfill-Aimeliik for a private scrap metal recycler for the purpose of scrap metal collection, treatment, and export at no cost to the government.",""],[1,"124","16","Private Company Recycler Incentive Scheme","Strengthen private company recyclers by providing incentives such as tax breaks.",""],[1,"124","17","Expanded Recycling Program for Non-Beverage Containers","Expand recycling program to include non- beverage containers",""]],"121":[[1,"124","6","Tipping Fee System Implementation","Tipping Fee system implemented by FY25.",""],[1,"124","15","National Landfill Tipping Fee System","Establish a Tipping Fee system at the National Landfill to support the Operations and Maintenance of the landfill.",""],[1,"123","4","Waste-to-Energy Technology Deployment","Waste-to-Energy technology would significantly reduce the volume of waste disposed at the landfill and at the same time produce usable energy.",""],[1,"124","21","Waste-to-Energy Feasibility Study","II.7 Feasibility study for Waste-to-Energy program",""]],"122":[[1,"126","1","National Tour Guide Certification Regulation","The national tour guide certification regulation is under preparation.",""],[1,"126","4","Tourism Statistics and Policy Analysis Support","More detailed tourism statistics are needed to help better understand the impact of tourism on the society and economy of Palau, including its current value-added and to otherwise assist policy planning.",""],[1,"126","4","International Tourism Market Research Initiative","International commercial market research is also needed to help Palau better understand what future tourism products and markets could meet the country's tourism goal.",""],[1,"126","4","Regular Tourism Policy Analysis and Advisory Support","Palau could greatly benefit from regular and updated commercial tourism development policy analyses and advice.",""],[1,"126","5","Tourism Impact Data Consultancy","this can be carried through as a priority program and project for 2023-2026.","FIB | Social Security | the Ministry of Finance"],[1,"127","5","International Tourism Products and Markets Research Consultancy","Recruitment of international tourism products and markets' research and development consultancy to help define new tourism policy and statistics.",""],[1,"127","7","Intermittent Tourism Policy Planning Adviser Recruitment","Recruitment of an intermittent tourism policy planning adviser.",""],[1,"128","6","Tourism Development Policy","A new Tourism Development Policy endorsed by OEK",""],[1,"128","8","National Tourism Policy and Statistics Framework","New national Tourism policy and set of statistics.",""],[1,"128","8","Tourism Value-Added Assessment Report","Report on assessment of tourism value- added.",""],[1,"128","13","Private Sector Engagement in Tourism Policy Development","The entire private sector is organized and can be engaged in the development of a new tourism development policy and strategy.",""],[1,"131","7","Tourism Policy and Strategy","New tourism policy and strategy put in place.",""],[1,"131","7","Private-Sector Tourism Product Development and Marketing Support","Private-sector tourism product development and marketing continue to support the restoration of the tourism industry.",""]],"123":[[1,"127","2","Cultural Tourism Development and Heritage Revival","There also needs to be a revival of Palauan arts and culture.",""],[1,"127","2","Cultural Learning Curriculum Integration","Not only will this involve the Historic Preservation Office with historical registered sites but also the school system to establish a cultural learning part of the curriculum and the community in passing hands-on skills and knowledge.",""],[1,"127","11","Tourism Destination Development for Ngeremiengul Waterfall, Ngchesar Waterfall, and Ngiwal Park","The development of Ngeremiengul waterfall, Ngchesar Waterfall, and Ngiwal Park as tourist destinations.",""],[1,"128","8","Annual Palauan Arts and Culture Events in Each State","At least one Palauan arts and culture event in each State, each year from FY 25 to FY 27.",""]],"124":[[1,"126","7","Small Business Advisory and Assistance Support","The government will continue to advise and otherwise assist small domestic businesses through the Small Business Development Center and the National Development Bank of Palau.",""],[1,"127","8","Infrastructure and Services Standards Establishment","· Establish standards for infrastructure and services.",""],[1,"127","9","Participatory Policy Dissemination and Consultation Program","A program of participatory workshops, other meetings, and policy dissemination.",""],[1,"128","8","Infrastructure and Services Standards Publication","Published standards for infrastructure and services.",""]],"125":[[1,"129","1","Air Transport Service Maintenance and Certification Programme","This includes maintaining our certification with continuous training for Aircraft Rescue and Fire Fighting, Airport Police, Automatic Flight Information Service Unit, Navigational Aide Technicians, and Airfield and Facilities Maintenance Personnel.",""],[1,"130","2","ICAO SARPS Compliance Improvement","Palau needs to continue to work towards addressing the International and Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO) SARPS (Standards and Recommended Practices) based on the 2010 ICAO audit.",""],[1,"130","3","Peleliu and Angaur Airfield Safety Upgrades","The Peleliu and Angaur airfields need to be developed to meet basic safety standards.",""],[1,"130","5","Airfield Operations and Maintenance Support","Support the operation and maintenance of Angaur and Peleliu Airfields.",""],[1,"130","5","ARFF and Airport Police Training and Recertification","Finance basic training and recertification for ARFF and Airport Police to maintain safety and security standards.",""],[1,"130","6","Airport Rescue Firefighting Building Refurbishment","Refurbish, renovate and repair the Airport Rescue Firefighting building.",""],[1,"130","7","Rescue Equipment and Firefighting Gear Acquisition","Acquire new rescue equipment and firefighting gear.",""],[1,"130","8","VHF Radio Procurement","Acquire a new VHF base and handheld radios.",""],[1,"130","9","Air Service Facilities and Airport Personnel Certification","To plan for and build air service facilities, and certification of airport personnel to maintain the safety and regulatory environment as the demand for air services increases.",""],[1,"130","14","Airfield Runway Safety Development","Peleliu and Angaur Airfields need to be developed to maintain runway safety measures.",""],[1,"131","8","Airport Firefighting and Security Training Recertification","Recertification of ARFF Training, Basic Training, and Continuous Recruitment Recertification of Airport Police Live Fire Training and Execution Security Program Assessment Completion of Personnel Leadership Training Completion of ACM, AEP, WHMP, and ALP Coordination and Cooperation on Joint Use Agreement with the US Increasing Air Transport Service with AP Region Extension of Runway to meet large aircraft",""],[1,"131","8","Airport Joint Use Agreement Coordination","Coordination and Cooperation on Joint Use Agreement with the US",""],[1,"131","21","Peleliu and Angaur Airfields Development","III.2 Develop Peleliu and Angaur Airfields",""],[1,"138","21","Replacement and Expansion of Light Aids and New Beacon Installation","Replace and extend light aids and place new beacons",""]],"126":[[1,"129","5","Public-Private Partnership Airport Terminal Expansion Project","The government's first public-private partnership project approved in early 2017 constructed a new annex building, and departure building and renovated the existing building to the main arrival building.",""],[1,"130","15","Airport Runway and Taxiway Surface Resealing","The international airport's existing runway and taxiways will require a surface reseal during the period of the PDP.",""],[1,"130","16","International Airport Renovation Project","a project involving major renovations to the international airport, including additional new gates with an estimated cost of $40 million funded by JICA/JBIC/SMBC is currently under implementation",""],[1,"130","16","Airport Security and Customs Modernization Expansion","A proposal to expand the scope of this project by including X-Ray equipment and a computerized Customs management system (ASYCUDA) at a cost of $5 million, is also currently under consideration",""],[1,"130","17","Aircraft Registry Establishment Legislation","· Establish Aircraft Registry through Legislation",""],[1,"131","8","Airport Air Transport Service Expansion","Increasing Air Transport Service with AP Region",""],[1,"131","8","Runway Extension for Large Aircraft","Extension of Runway to meet large aircraft",""],[1,"131","22","International Airport Runway and Taxiway Resealing","Reseal international airport's runway and taxiways",""],[1,"149","3","Palau International Airport Renovation and Expansion","The government and Japan Airport Terminal Company (JATCO) signed a joint venture agreement in August 2017 to renovate and expand the Palau International Airport.",""],[1,"151","3","National Airport Expansion","The government was also set to receive a $10.2 million grant from the FAA to expand the national airport.",""],[1,"152","4","Palau International Airport Renovation, Expansion, and Operation","Renovation, expansion, and operation of Palau International Airport",""],[1,"151","7","Australia-Palau Connector Flight Route","A new flight, the \"Australia-Palau Connector\" connecting Brisbane, Port Moresby, and Koror return commenced in December 2022.",""]],"127":[[1,"132","6","Roads, Causeways, and Bridges Network Expansion","To slowly build up the roads, causeways, and bridges network and associated safety and regulatory environment as the demand for land transport increases.",""],[1,"133","2","Koror-Airai Road Repairs","· Desing of Koror-Airai road repairs",""],[1,"133","4","State Road Paving Programme","Paving the roads from each state that connect to the Compact Road or to communities within a state will remain a priority for the duration of the plan",""],[1,"133","5","Minato Bridge Preparatory Study and New Bridge Construction","Minato Bridge Preparatory Study and construction of a new bridge",""],[1,"133","6","Culvert Replacement on Malakal and Meyuns Causeways","Replacement of culverts on Malakal and Meyuns causeways",""],[1,"133","7","Pedestrian Walkway Rehabilitation and Construction in Koror","Rehabilitate or build new pedestrian walkways in Koror.",""],[1,"133","8","Periodic Road Area Repair Programme","Periodic repair of random road areas to prevent premature pavement impairment",""],[1,"134","5","Rural Road Upgrading to Reinforced Concrete","All roads in rural areas of Babeldaob connecting to the Compact Road are improved with reinforced Portland cement concrete.",""],[1,"134","5","Interstate Village Road Paving Programme","All interstate roads connecting villages within states are paved as mentioned above.",""],[1,"134","5","Bridge and Culvert Rehabilitation on Causeways","Main bridges and culverts on causeways are renewed/improved to ensure vehicular traffic safety and extended service life of infrastructure.",""],[1,"142","13","Ngerimel Bridge Reconstruction","Re-construction of Ngerimel Bridge which is used by the Koror-Airai Water Treatment Plant personnel to cross to the other side for dams, wells, and transmission lines valves maintenance.",""],[1,"144","7","Ngerimel Bridge Reconstruction","Ngerimel Bridge re-constructed.",""],[1,"155","15","Ngerimel Bridge Reconstruction","Re-Construction of Ngerimel Bridge",""],[1,"152","7","Japan-Palau Friendship Bridge Construction","Construction of the Japan-Palau Friendship Bridge",""]],"128":[[1,"133","3","Climate-Proofing of Low-Lying Roads and Causeways","Climate-proofing of low-lying roads and causeways.",""],[1,"133","11","Public Transportation Investment Options","the government will also examine options to invest in public transportation, with the objective of reducing congestion and CO2 emissions.",""],[1,"133","12","Technical Training for Development Planning and Inspection","Technical training (in person and virtual) in development planning, construction inspection, maintenance inspections",""],[1,"133","13","Technical Maintenance Training","Technical training on maintenance",""],[1,"134","8","Project Documentation and Supplemental Project Details Preparation","Project Documentation and Supplemental Project Details write-up and submission to funding agencies.",""],[1,"134","8","Project Inception and Delivery Arrangement Planning","Project inception planning including the determination of whether to outsource projects, perform them in-house or perform thru Force Account Agreements with State Governments.",""],[1,"134","8","Project Scope, Procurement, and Construction Management Support","Development of project scope of works and bill of quantities needed for procurement purposes or in-house implementation or force account.",""],[1,"134","8","Project Handover to Owning Stakeholder","Handover of the completed project to owning stakeholder.",""]],"129":[[1,"135","1","Domestic Implementation of Maritime Rules and Policies","to provide a safe, secure, and healthy maritime environment through domestic implementation of applicable maritime rules and policies.",""],[1,"135","4","Purpose-Built Passenger/Cargo Vessel Procurement and Operation","it is recommended that a larger purpose-built passenger/cargo vessel, preferably with twin engines and bow thrusters, be procured, and operated with one of the existing smaller vessels to unify these services and to reduce the cost of personnel and maintenance.",""],[1,"135","4","Multi-Purpose National Government Vessel Service","The vessel can be operated by the national government as a multi-purpose vessel.",""],[1,"135","4","Training Ship for Local Seafarers","it can also serve as a training ship to train local seafarers for work on the larger domestic passenger vessels and to support the government's efforts in maintaining aids to navigation.",""],[1,"137","6","Government-Owned Inter-Island Passenger Ship Service","The government intends to increase its role in the marine transport sector to improve marine transport services by (i) replacing a less efficient private sector fleet of small vessels servicing the islands with one larger government-owned and operated ship",""],[1,"137","7","Government Vessel Feasibility Study and Investment","Feasibility study followed by the investment and operation of a government vessel",""],[1,"138","5","Government-Owned Maritime Transport Service Upgrade","Increased government role in the maritime transport sector to improve maritime transport services by (i) replacing a less efficient private sector fleet of small vessels servicing the islands with one larger government-owned and operated ship, thereby creating a mechanism for seafarer training, and maintaining navigation aids.",""],[1,"138","8","Government-Owned Vessel Operations","The government-owned and operated vessel commences operation and provides increased maritime transport services to all islands at a lower cost than previous operations.",""],[1,"136","5","Temporary Reefer Container Power Support at Malakal Port","In case of emergencies, generators can be provided for temporary power needs.",""],[1,"137","9","Malakal Commercial Port Expansion and Rehabilitation","Feasibility study followed by the expansion and Rehabilitation of Malakal Commercial Port",""],[1,"138","5","Malakal Port Rehabilitation and Expansion","rehabilitating the existing port in Malakal to increase the land area by acquiring adjacent fisheries dock, as indicated by a) stabilized freight rates as the port will be able to handle larger and more cost-efficient vessels, and b) an increase in luxury yacht visits.",""],[1,"138","8","Extended Malakal Port Development","Extended Malakal port provides increased port services at a lower cost than previous operations.",""]],"130":[[1,"136","1","Maritime Aids to Navigation and Search and Rescue Services","Palau has an obligation to provide Aids to Navigation, weather forecasts, up-to-date and corrected hydrographic charts, and maritime search and rescue services.",""],[1,"137","2","Marine Navigation Aids Rehabilitation and Replacement","Through grant funding assistance from partner countries, the Bureau of Marine Transportation has been able to replace all floating aids and is undertaking the rehabilitation of 85 beacon markers.",""],[1,"137","2","Beacon Marker Replacement and Upgrade Programme","there remain about 115 beacon markers, range markers, and light beacons that need to be replaced or upgraded to ensure the safety of navigation.",""],[1,"137","6","Waterway Marking and Navigation Aids Programme","The government will also continue to mark the entrances of all state waterways with lighted aids and mark all risks to navigation.",""],[1,"137","10","West Pass Range Marker Replacement","Replace two sets of range markers in West Pass",""],[1,"137","11","Malakal Harbor Light Aid Replacement","Replace light aid in Malakal Harbor",""],[1,"137","12","Light Aid Extension at East Pass","Extend light aid in front of East Pass",""],[1,"137","13","State Waterway Beacon Installation","Install 115 new beacons in state waterways",""]],"131":[[1,"137","4","National Drydock Facility Development and Operation","it is recommended that Palau Government build and operate a drydock facility at a suitable location to accommodate vessels of up to 500GT.",""],[1,"137","5","Local Shipyard Development","This amount, less fuel cost, can be invested locally if there was a fully functional shipyard that could accommodate these vessels.",""],[1,"137","6","Drydock Feasibility Assessment","investigating the potential viability of investing in a drydock",""],[1,"137","6","Malakal Port Rehabilitation and Seafarer Training Facility","rehabilitating the existing port in Malakal to increase the land area by acquiring the adjacent fisheries dock, and thereby create a mechanism for seafarer training",""],[1,"137","8","Dry-dock Facility Feasibility Study and Construction","Feasibility study followed by the construction of a Dry-dock Facility",""],[1,"138","5","Public Drydock Service Development","a Palau drydock supplying a lower cost service than existing domestic and Philippine drydocks.",""],[1,"138","8","Government-Owned Drydock Operations","The government-owned (and possibly private sector- operated) drydock commences operation and provides services at a lower cost.",""]],"132":[[1,"139","5","Integrated Water Supply and Distribution System Upgrades","Water systems need improvements along their entire supply and distribution chain, from watershed rehabilitation to sourcing of new above- and below-ground water sources to improved water treatment to improved and expanded water distribution systems that maintain potable water quality until it reaches the end user.",""],[1,"139","5","Babeldaob State Water System Consolidation","On Babeldaob Island, removing the individual burden of water systems from States is a high priority, and with many large rivers producing more than enough",""],[1,"140","1","Integrated Water Supply System Development","there is a desire to see the development of a single, large, modern, and fully integrated water supply system as is seen in Koror and parts of Airai.",""],[1,"142","7","Water Infrastructure Investment and Utility Efficiency Improvements","The government is investing in new plants and gradually raising tariffs to reduce subsidies, adopting new, more appropriate ownership, and has taken action to strengthen water and sewer management and to otherwise seek to improve operational efficiencies and effectiveness.",""],[1,"142","10","Rural Water Pumping Station and Distribution System Rehabilitation","The rehabilitation of rural water pumping stations and distribution systems.",""],[1,"142","11","Rural Water System Expansion","Expansion of rural water systems to new homes and subdivisions.",""],[1,"142","12","Water Desalination Plant Rehabilitation","The rehabilitation of water desalination plants",""],[1,"143","1","Ngerikiil Dam Weir Raising and Wall Reconstruction","Raise the existing Ngerikiil Dam Weir by 2ft and re-construct the Ngerikiil Dam Walls to stop leakage and increase volume capacity.",""],[1,"143","2","Distribution Storage Tank Refurbishment","Refurbishing of the Distribution Storage Tanks in Airai, Ngermid, Ngerkesoal, and Ngerkebesang.",""],[1,"144","7","Distribution Storage Tank Refurbishment","Airai, Ngermid, Ngekesoaol, and Ngerkebesang Distribution Storage Tanks refurbished.",""],[1,"144","24","Distribution Storage Tank Refurbishment","III.5 Refurbish the Distribution Storage Tanks - Airai, Ngermid, Ngerkesoaol, and Ngerkebesang",""],[1,"146","19","Distribution Storage Tank Refurbishment","Refurbish the Distribution Storage Tanks - Airai, Ngermid, Ngerkesoaol, and Ngerkebesang",""],[1,"155","16","Distribution Storage Tank Refurbishment","Refurbish the Distribution Storage Tanks - Airai, Ngermid, Ngerkesoaol, and Ngerkebesang",""],[1,"143","3","Peleliu Water Treatment Facility Reconstruction and Reinforcement","Reconstruction and reinforcement of Peleliu Water Treatment concrete walling of the existing 60,000 gallons underground holding tank to avoid further damage to the walling around the underground holding tank.",""],[1,"143","4","Water System Improvement Projects","Various water system improvement projects for Imeong, Ngeremlengui, Mechebechubel, Ngatpang, Mongami & Ngchemiangel Aimeliik.",""],[1,"143","5","Feasibility Study for an Integrated Water System","Feasibility study for the creation of a single, integrated water system for Babeldaob's rural states.",""],[1,"144","7","Koror-Airai Water System Rehabilitation","Koror - Airai System rehabilitated.",""],[1,"144","7","Climate-Resilient Household Water Connection Expansion","Proportion of new homes connected to public water system and/or with climate- resilient tank systems that regularly meet minimum water quality standards increased.",""],[1,"144","17","Feasibility Studies and Technical Planning for Water System Expansion","Feasibility studies/Technical planning for expansion of existing water systems into new subdivisions",""],[1,"144","18","Feasibility Study for New Centralized Babeldaob Water System","Feasibility study for new, centralized Babeldaob Water System",""],[1,"144","23","Ngerikiil Dam Weir Raising and Dam Wall Reconstruction","Raise Ngerikiil Dam Weir by 2ft and reconstruct Dam Walls",""],[1,"147","3","Ngerikiil Dam Weir Raising and Dam Wall Reconstruction","Raise Ngerikiil Dam Weir by 2ft and reconstruct Dam Walls",""],[1,"155","19","Ngerikiil Dam Weir Raising and Dam Wall Reconstruction","Raise Ngerikiil Dam Weir by 2ft and reconstruct Dam Walls",""],[1,"144","25","Water System Improvement Project","Water system improvement project for Imeong Ngeremlengui, Mechebechubel Ngatpang, Mongami and Ngchemiangel Aimeliik",""],[1,"147","1","Water System Improvement Project","Water system improvement project for Imeong Ngeremlengui, Mechebechubel Ngatpang, Mongami and Ngchemiangel Aimeliik",""],[1,"155","17","Water System Improvement Project","Water system improvement project for Imeong Ngeremlengui, Mechebechubel Ngatpang, Mongami and Ngchemiangel Aimeliik",""]],"133":[[1,"140","4","Koror Wastewater Network Interconnection Works","The sewage pump stations' interconnection and network interconnection works are pending.",""],[1,"140","4","Koror Pump Station Refurbishment and Rehabilitation","Some of the pump stations need refurbishment, including the replacement of internal plumbing, valves, and control panels.",""],[1,"140","4","Koror Pump Station Structural Rehabilitation and Relocation","Some pump stations require main sump structural rehabilitation work due to infiltration.",""],[1,"140","4","Relocation of Three Koror Pump Stations","Three pump stations need to be relocated as these are in or adjacent to private properties.",""],[1,"140","4","New Koror Wastewater Treatment Plant","A new wastewater treatment plant was designed, constructed, and commissioned in November 2021 with Sequential Batch Reactor technology.",""],[1,"140","5","Melekeok Wastewater Treatment Plant Upgrade","The plant will need to be upgraded to",""],[1,"144","28","Melekeok Wastewater Treatment Plant Upgrade","Upgrade of Melekeok Wastewater Treatment Plant with existing capacity and procurement of pumps and spare parts",""],[1,"141","2","Subdivision Sewage Treatment Design","Designing subdivisions to include sewage treatment is an immediate priority.",""],[1,"141","2","Sewer System Construction and Septic Tank Retrofitting","Due to cost, building sewer systems and retrofitting septic tanks is a long-term priority.",""],[1,"142","8","Koror-Airai Sanitation Project Phase II","A second phase of the latter project is planned.",""],[1,"142","9","Koror-Airai System Rehabilitation","The rehabilitation of the Koror-Airai system.",""],[1,"143","9","Melekeok Treatment Plant Renovation and Expansion","The renovation and expansion of the Melekeok treatment plant",""],[1,"143","10","Rural Sewage Pumping Station and Collection Pipe Rehabilitation","The replacement and rehabilitation of sewage pumping stations and collection pipes in rural areas.",""],[1,"143","11","Technical Planning Support for Septic Tank Suitability","Assistance with technical planning to ensure septic tanks are fit-for-purpose per location/subdivision.",""],[1,"143","12","Feasibility Study for Septic Tank Conversion to Sewage Systems","This will be implemented via a feasibility study for the conversion of septic tanks to sewage systems in rural states and subdivisions.",""],[1,"143","12","Alternative Sewage Disposal Methods Assessment","the government will examine alternative methods of sewage disposal, such as Kubota treatment plants, which are highly efficient and environmentally friendly.",""],[1,"144","31","Koror Wastewater Pumping Station Refurbishment","Refurbishment of the 37 Koror wastewater pumping stations.",""]],"134":[[1,"142","4","Water and Sewerage Tariff Reform for Full Cost Recovery","A framework of tariffs and tariff increases to achieve full cost recovery has been agreed upon and is being implemented.",""],[1,"142","5","Emergency Repair and Maintenance of Water Supply Backup Generators","This is a serious deficiency that needs to be urgently addressed.",""],[1,"142","7","Water Management Legislative and Regulatory Reform","The government seeks to further amend legislation and regulations in support of improved water management.",""],[1,"144","12","Tariff Reform to Enable Sustainable Systems","Political support for increased tariffs to enable sustainable system.",""]],"135":[[1,"145","1","Infrastructure Approval and Capital Expenditure Prioritization Process","The Palau NIIP138 adopted a 5-stage process of infrastructure approval that can now be applied to all capital expenditures: (i) compile a long list of all proposed capital expenditures, (ii) assess each proposal's readiness for appraisal, (iii) approve the Multi- Criteria Analysis (MCA) criteria, (iv) use the MCA to score proposals that are ready for appraisal and prioritize them, and (v) seek funding.",""],[1,"145","3","CAPEX Committee Clearance Process","all capital expenditure should first be cleared by a \"CAPEX Committee\"","the Attorney General's Office | the Ministry of Finance | the Office of Human Resources | the Ministry of Public Infrastructure and Industries | the Ministries of Health and Education | the Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries and the Environment | the Bureau of Land and Survey"],[1,"146","2","Capital Expenditure Prioritization Framework","Capital expenditures are prioritized regardless of funding source; that is, whether they are to be funded from domestic revenues or possibly donor or development partner financed.",""],[1,"154","4","National Infrastructure Investment Plan Finalization","The Pacific Region Infrastructure Facility helped Palau finalize its National Infrastructure Investment Plan, which set priorities for investments during 2021-2030.",""],[1,"157","1","Sector Performance Monitoring and Funding Framework Updates","PDP progress will be annually monitored at the sector level when each sector performance monitoring and funding framework is updated every April to June in preparation for annual budget negotiations.",""]],"136":[[1,"148","1","Development Plan Financing Mobilization Framework","The potential sources of PDP funding are (i) the national government's own revenues and borrowing, (ii) local, state government revenues and borrowing, state-owned enterprises (SOEs) and other revenue-retaining institutions, (iii) donor grants, (iv) development partner loans, (v) climate funds, and (vi) private sector investments including Public-Private Partnerships (PPPs).",""],[1,"149","2","Public-Private Partnership Framework Preparation","Subprogram 2 of the policy-based loan from ADB aims to assist the government in preparing a framework for PPP.",""],[1,"149","6","Public-Private Partnership Expansion","The government is considering further PPPs including partnerships in domestic commercial tuna fishing.",""],[1,"149","6","PPP Development in Tourism and Port Infrastructure","Future PPPs might also be considered in tourism, vessel slipway construction, and port development.",""],[1,"150","4","Compact Renewal and Economic Assistance Agreement","Palau's COFA has now been reviewed and renewed and an agreement between the two governments was signed in Port Moresby on May 2023.",""],[1,"150","4","Continued Grant Assistance Support","The terms originally specified in the Compact Renewal Agreement were for continuing current grant assistance, although at a declining level.",""],[1,"150","4","CTF, Infrastructure Maintenance, and Capital Projects Funding","Additional resources were provided to support the CTF, infrastructure maintenance, and capital projects.",""],[1,"151","2","COFA Funding Allocation for Priority Public Purposes","the new COFA is to be used exclusively for purposes related to education, health, climate adaptation, and the environment, the administration of justice, and public safety or for expenses related to required audits.",""],[1,"151","4","Aid Coordination Unit","The establishment of an Aid Coordination Unit will help the government manage the various donor assistance programs in the interest of national development priorities and coordinate and integrate capital with recurrent budget management.",""],[1,"152","10","Aid Coordination Unit","The establishment of an Aid Coordination Unit will help the government manage the various development partner assistance programs in the interest of national development priorities and coordinate and integrate capital with recurrent budget management.",""],[1,"151","5","Post-ODA Support Funding for Palau","The Government of Australia allocated $4 million per year from 2022 to 2023 in non-ODA funds to support Palau after it graduated from the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development's (OECD) List of Official Development Assistance (ODA).",""],[1,"154","7","Aid Coordination Unit for Project Funding and Budget Prioritization","Future project funding will be coordinated by the new Aid Coordination Unit and all future capital and recurrent expenditure financing will be administered, filtered, scored and ranked in accordance with future budget preparations for each fiscal year.",""],[1,"154","6","Government Revenue Generation Strategy","The PDP and longer-term funding strategy for development expenditure prioritizes the generation of government revenues so that the government may in the future finance its priority investments from its own funds.",""],[1,"154","6","Revenue-Generating Development Studies","This will include priority projects of a recurrent nature, such as policy, planning, market research, management and feasibility studies that will help identify revenue-generating development activities.",""]],"137":[[1,"150","1","PPUC Corporate Governance and Financial Management Strengthening","The loan to PPUC will strengthen the utility's corporate governance and financial management to ensure sustainable service delivery.",""],[1,"150","1","Technical Assistance for BSCC and PNCC Operations","the World Bank is planning to provide technical assistance to strengthen the operations of BSCC and PNCC.",""],[1,"151","6","ICT Sector Reform and Affordable Internet Access","Australia supported development activities to (ii) reform Palau's ICT sector and increase access to high-quality, low-cost internet services",""],[1,"153","1","Utility and Public Sector Performance Capacity Support","Recognizing the need for capacity support to complement physical infrastructure, ADB is helping improve utility and public sector performance alongside infrastructure works.",""],[1,"153","7","Technical Assistance for ICT Sector Operations and Infrastructure Planning","The World Bank has assisted Palau with ICT and oil and gas exploration and is planning to provide technical assistance to strengthen the operations of BSCC and PNCC to analyze additional ICT infrastructure needs with possible financing to use the international submarine cable more effectively, and to promote sector growth and development158.",""],[1,"155","10","Fiber-Optic Cable Expansion","Expansion of fiber -optic cable",""],[1,"155","12","SCADA Software System Update","Update SCADA software system",""]],"138":[[1,"146","16","Construction and Furnishing of the New Prison in Ngchesar","Complete construction of and furnishings for the new Prison in Ngchesar",""],[1,"155","13","New Prison Construction and Furnishing in Ngchesar","Complete construction of and furnishings for the new Prison in Ngchesar",""],[1,"151","6","Unexploded Ordnance Clearance Programme","Australia supported development activities to (i) remove unexploded ordnance from Koror and Peleliu, freeing land and marine areas for infrastructure, agriculture, housing, tourism, and community use",""],[1,"153","6","Border Management Support for COVID-19 Recovery and Preparedness","The UNDP also plans to assist Palau, together with Fiji, Samoa, and Vanuatu, with border management in support of COVID-19 recovery and preparedness.",""]],"139":[[1,"149","5","Integrated Greenhouse PPP for Agriculture and Aquaculture","Palau Nature Works (PNW), the subsidiary of Guam Nature Works (GNW), and Aimeliik State Government signed a PPP Agreement to build integrated greenhouses for both agriculture and aquaculture farm operations in Aimeliik, Palau (year unknown).",""],[1,"152","5","Renovation of Palau Mariculture Demonstration Center","Renovation of Palau Mariculture Demonstration Center",""],[1,"152","6","Palau International Coral Reef Research Center Construction","Construction of the Palau International Coral Reef Research Center",""],[1,"154","1","Blue Prosperity Plan Implementation Support","currently processing an investment project and technical assistance in support of the implementation of the Blue Prosperity Plan for approval late 2024.",""]],"140":[[1,"152","8","Housing Loan Facility","The Republic of China is preparing a further housing loan of $15 million.",""],[1,"154","4","Business Environment Strengthening Initiative","The Pacific Private Sector Development Initiative is strengthening the business environment by supporting PPPs, increased transparency, and improved access to credit.",""]],"141":[[1,"153","4","Recovery through Improved Systems and Expenditure Support Program","In 2022, ADB provided budget support loans under the Recovery through Improved Systems and Expenditure Support (RISES) Program (Subprogram 2) and Palau Public Utilities Corporation (PPUC) (Phase 2) with $30 million and $5 million, respectively.",""],[1,"153","4","Palau Public Utilities Corporation Governance and Financial Management Strengthening","The loan to PPUC will strengthen the utility's corporate governance and financial management to ensure sustainable service delivery.",""]],"142":[[1,"151","6","Tertiary Qualification Support Programme","Australia supported development activities to (iii) assist 22 Palauans to gain tertiary qualifications",""]]}});